dy know how you plan to impact the world or whether you are still trying to decide what do after your degree, know that Nova SBE has a program that will guide you all the way through your Masters’ program. The Nova SBE Career Services team runs a comprehensive program that provides you with the necessary tools to help taking the next step more effectively from day one and transform your uncertainties into bold aspirations that can really make a difference. To help students throughout the process, the Nova SBE Career Services teams's offer includes: 96% working after 3 months 100% working after 6 months 67% with an international career Career Program The Career Program offers a comprehensive series of activities - including workshops, career events, and company networking opportunities - designed to help you build market knowledge and define your personal and professional goals. Through targeted skill development, you will be equipped to become a highly competitive candidate and a thoughtful, well-rounded professional. 1:1 Career Counselling You will deepen your knowledge about yourself and use that insight to make more informed decisions about your next steps. In 1:1 career counselling sessions, you’ll get guidance when you’re unsure and practical support to help you prepare for job interviews and navigate recruitment processes. Career Fairs Two exclusive events to meet and network with recruiters from leading international and national companies. Corporate Events By joining Corporate Events, you’ll meet employers and alumni, learn what different companies and organizations are really like, and get a better understanding of today’s job market. Career Center by JobTeaser The JobTeaser portal, from the Nova SBE Career Services team, connects students to the job market, providing access to job offers and corporate and career events. Career Mentoring Program The Career Mentoring Program is an optional service that pairs you with a Nova SBE alumni mentor, giving you access to real-world perspectives, honest guidance, and a network that goes beyond the classroom - all to support your career development and help you navigate your next steps with confidence. Online Tools To support you throughout your career journey, you will have access to a wide range of resources covering every stage of the process — from crafting a compelling CV and cover letter, to mastering networking, preparing for interviews, and navigating your job search. Our online tools, including JobTeaser, Career Set, Big Interview, Graduate First, and Case Coach, are available to help you research the market, connect with opportunities, and put your best foot forward at every step. Most popular sectors Serviços Financeiros Consultoria Some companies that recruit at Nova SBE Bain & Company Bank of America Boston Consulting Group BNP Paribas Carlsquare Deloitte European Central Bank EY Parthenon Kearney KPMG Nordea PwC Roland Berger Rothschild & Co Unicredit Where are we To find out about all the ways the Nova SBE Career Services  team can support you and other helpful information, meet us at our office D124. Office Hours Monday to Friday, from 10.00 am to 1.00 pm Are you ready to embrace the future? Good choices can change the course of the future. Deciding what you want for your future is never easy, but Nova SBE can help you. To offer students a chance to discover where they can excel and have a meaningful career, we also share OBIPNOVA . This is a NOVA University Lisbon’s Rectory initiative that involves all NOVA schools. It aims to produce information about the career trajectory of all NOVA students regardless of their study cycle. Every year, it evaluates the professional activity of those who graduated to provide the NOVA community rigorous and reliable indicators about the career and placement of its graduates’ achievements. Learn all about OBIPNOVA here Share Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Email Contacts Contacts & Directions Ecosystem Students Alumni Research Knowled