ts Students Instructors People Contacts Inclusive Community Forum Back Inclusive Community Forum Overview Community Employability Back Employability Overview Inclusive Journey Recruitment Peer2Peer Process Education Back Education Overview Inclusion Labs Process Empower to Employ Inclusion Projects Team Contacts Press Clipping VCW Lab Back VCW Lab Overview Projects Education Publications People Nova SBE Teaching & Innovation Center Back Nova SBE Teaching & Innovation Center About us Our offer Faculty Hub Project-Based Learning Teaching Excellence Community Impact Get Involved Institutes Back Institutes Nova SBE Haddad Entrepreneurship Institute Back Nova SBE Haddad Entrepreneurship Institute Overview Students Startups Research People What’s Happening Contacts Mentors Network Nova SBE Westmont Institute of Tourism & Hospitality Back Nova SBE Westmont Institute of Tourism & Hospitality Overview Education Global Research Societal Outreach Africa People Contacts Digital Data Design Institute Back Digital Data Design Institute Overview AI X Lab Learning Pathways Join as a partner! People Events Contacts News Nova SBE Public Policy Institute Life at Nova SBE Overview About the campus Getting started Student Support Community Engagement Well-being FAQ International Students Nova Way of Life What's Happening Newsroom Back Newsroom Overview Specialists Media Kit Contacts Press Releases News Events RRP @ Nova SBE Master's Programs International Master's in Finance Overview Program Fees Careers Scholarships & Funding Apply Study Abroad Numbers over words Nova SBE Career Services Starting the International Master’s in Finance at Nova SBE is one of the first steps towards a successful international career. The International Master's in Finance is considered the 6th best International Master's in Finance by the Financial Times. Also, did you know that 100 % of our graduates are working within six months of graduating, and that 81 % of those have an international career? The Nova SBE Career Services team, whose vision is to Empower Meaningful and Sustainable Careers, is committed to guide you and provide you with key resources when planning your professional path.  As an International Master’s in Finance student, you will have access to an exclusive career program adapted to your personal needs and interests. IMF&IMM Career Program The IMF&IMM Career Program, will help you acquire market knowledge and set your career plan. Through the attendance at group workshops, individual career advising sessions, and exclusive networking events with international companies, this program allows you to acquire the skills that will empower you to become the most knowledgeable candidate and conscious professional. All the career guidance is structured considering 4 main industries (Financial Services, Consulting, Consumer Goods and Technology), with a focus on 4 main pillars: Self-awareness, Knowledge about the market, Networking and Recruitment processes. Individual Career Advising sessions In this journey, you will be accompanied by a dedicated Career Consultant who will guide and support you in defining your career goals and preparing you for the recruitment processes. Career Fairs Two exclusive events to meet and network with recruiters from leading  international companies. Career Events We offer activities both on-campus (company presentations, business challenges, networking opportunities) and off-campus (company visits, online presentations). Careers@ Our Careers@ are field visits to companies of a specific geography, so that you connect with these companies and understand how it is to work in this specific location. Career Center by JobTeaser The Nova SBE Career Services portal by JobTeaser connects students to the marketplace, by providing access to Job Offers, Events, Counselling, and Career-related resources. Online Tools Students have exclusive and free access to other platforms that will support career planning and market knowledge, such as, CaseCoach, Graduate First and Big Interview. Students will also have access to a Career Portal designed to provide you with valuable resources to navigate your career preparation journey. We have centralized a variety of career preparation tools to make your search easier and provide you with the guidance you need. Career Opportunities Mastering International Masters in Finance at Nova SBE will get you places Supported by Nova SBE throughout their Master’s studies, graduates make their first steps into working life in a wide variety of sectors, positions, companies, and countries. Also, did you know that 100 % of our graduates are working within six months of graduating and around 81 % of those have an international career? 83,3 % working after 3 months 100 % working after 6 months 81% with an international career Most popular sectors Financial Services Consulting Top 10 Recruiters Bain & Company BNP Paribas CIB BCG Deloitte J.P. Morgan Morgan Stanley McKinsey & Company Nomura Oliver Wyman UBS Most popular placement countries Germany Portugal Switzerland United Kingdom Spain Austria Belgium France Luxembourg Where are we To find out about all the ways the Nova SBE Career Services  team can support you and other helpful information, meet us at our office D124. Office Hours Monday to Friday, from 10.00 am to 1.00 pm Contact (+351) 213 822 792 careers@novasbe.pt Are you ready to embrace the future? Good choices can change the course of the future. Deciding what you want for your future is never easy, but Nova SBE can help you. To offer students a chance to discover where they can excel and have a meaningful career, we also share OBIPNOVA . This is a NOVA University Lisbon’s Rectory initiative that involves all NOVA schools. It aims to produce information about the career trajectory of all NOVA students regardless of their study cycle. Every year, it evaluates the professional activity of those who graduated to provide the NOVA community rigorous and reliable indicators 