jects Students Instructors People Contacts Inclusive Community Forum Back Inclusive Community Forum Overview Community Employability Back Employability Overview Inclusive Journey Recruitment Peer2Peer Process Education Back Education Overview Inclusion Labs Process Empower to Employ Inclusion Projects Team Contacts Press Clipping VCW Lab Back VCW Lab Overview Projects Education Publications People Nova SBE Teaching & Innovation Center Back Nova SBE Teaching & Innovation Center About us Our offer Faculty Hub Project-Based Learning Teaching Excellence Community Impact Get Involved Institutes Back Institutes Nova SBE Haddad Entrepreneurship Institute Back Nova SBE Haddad Entrepreneurship Institute Overview Students Startups Research People What’s Happening Contacts Mentors Network Nova SBE Westmont Institute of Tourism & Hospitality Back Nova SBE Westmont Institute of Tourism & Hospitality Overview Education Global Research Societal Outreach Africa People Contacts Digital Data Design Institute Back Digital Data Design Institute Overview AI X Lab Learning Pathways Join as a partner! People Events Contacts News Nova SBE Public Policy Institute Life at Nova SBE Overview About the campus Getting started Student Support Community Engagement Well-being FAQ International Students Nova Way of Life What's Happening Newsroom Back Newsroom Overview Specialists Media Kit Contacts Press Releases News Events RRP @ Nova SBE Master's Programs International Master's in Management Overview Program Fees Careers Scholarships & Funding Apply Study Abroad Numbers over words Nova SBE Career Services Starting the International Master’s in Management at Nova SBE is one of the first steps towards a successful international career. The International Master's in Management is considered the 4th best International Master's in Management by the Financial Times. Also, did you know that 100 % of our graduates are working within six months of graduating, and that 78.8 % of those have an international career? The Nova SBE Career Services team, whose vision is to Empower Meaningful and Sustainable Careers, is committed to guide you and provide you with key resources when planning your professional path. As an International Master’s in Management student, you will have access to an exclusive career program adapted to your personal needs and interests. IMF&IMM Career Program The IMF&IMM Career Program helps you acquire market knowledge and set your career plan. Through group workshops, individual advising sessions, and exclusive networking events with international companies, this program empowers you to become a more knowledgeable and conscious professional, focusing on four pillars: self-awareness, market knowledge, networking, and recruitment processes. Individual Career Advising Sessions In this journey, you’ll be accompanied by a dedicated Career Consultant who will guide and support you in defining your goals and preparing for recruitment processes. Career Fairs Two exclusive events to meet and network with recruiters from leading international companies. Career Events We offer both on-campus activities (company presentations, challenges, networking) and off-campus opportunities (company visits, online presentations). Careers@ Our Careers@ are field visits to companies in specific geographies, helping you connect with organizations and understand their work environments. Career Center by JobTeaser The Nova SBE Career Services portal by JobTeaser connects students to the marketplace with access to job offers, events, counselling, and resources. Online Tools Students have exclusive and free access to platforms supporting career planning and market knowledge, such as CaseCoach, Graduate First, and Big Interview. Career Opportunities Mastering International Masters in Management at Nova SBE will get you places Supported by Nova SBE throughout their Master’s studies, graduates make their first steps into working life in a wide variety of sectors, positions, companies, and countries. Also, did you know that 100 % of our graduates are working within six months of graduating and around 78,8 % of those have an international career? 90,3 % working after 3 months 100% working after 6 months 78.8% with an international career Most popular sectors Consulting Consumer Goods Technology Top 10 Recruiters Amazon Accenture Bain & Company BCG Capgemini Invent Deloitte EY-Parthenon PwC Simon Kucher RBI Most popular placement countries Germany Portugal Switzerland Austria Belgium Italy Luxembourg Ireland Where are we To find out about all the ways the Nova SBE Career Services  team can support you and other helpful information, meet us at our office D124. Office Hours Monday to Friday, from 10.00 am to 1.00 pm Contact (+351) 213 822 792 careers@novasbe.pt Are you ready to embrace the future? Good choices can change the course of the future. Deciding what you want for your future is never easy, but Nova SBE can help you. To offer students a chance to discover where they can excel and have a meaningful career, we also share OBIPNOVA . This is a NOVA University Lisbon’s Rectory initiative that involves all NOVA schools. It aims to produce information about the career trajectory of all NOVA students regardless of their study cycle. Every year, it evaluates the professional activity of those who graduated to provide the NOVA community rigorous and reliable indicators about the career and placement of its graduates’ achievements. Learn all about OBIPNOVA here Share Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Email Contacts Contacts & Directions Ecosystem Students Alumni Research Knowledge Centers Shortcuts Join our School Regulations & Public Announcements Fundação Alfredo de Sousa Library Nova SBE Today Moodle@NovaSBE Webmail Student Hub Whistleblower Portal Follow us Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn Youtube Accredited by: Member of: Participant in: Recovery and Resilience Plan (RRP) Privacy Policy Cookies Policy Back to top"
