ols Back Summer Schools PHD Summer School Executive Education Back Executive Education Homepage Open Programs Back Open Programs Marketing, Sales & Operations Sustainability & Impact Leadership & Change Management Management & Strategy Finance & Economics AI Data Digital Innovation & Entrepreneurship Companies Program Finder Calendar Faculty Contact us Blog Faculty & Research Faculty Research Areas Back Research Areas Finance Economics Management Research Unit Back Research Unit Overview Projects Publications Impact Highlights Chairs PhD Programs Reports Knowledge Centers Back Knowledge Centers Data, Operations & Technology Back Data, Operations & Technology Overview X-Collider Education Projects Publications Opportunities Team Contacts Events News Economics for Policy Economics of Education Back Economics of Education News Projects Publications Overview Events People Contacts MSc & PhD Environmental Economics Back Environmental Economics Overview Publications Events News Contacts Projects People Finance Back Finance About Us Education Finance PHD Events Projects Research People Events News Contacts Health Economics & Management Back Health Economics & Management Overview Contacts Events People News Publications Projects Leadership for Impact Back Leadership for Impact Overview People Projects Contacts Get involved Research Reports NOVAFRICA Back NOVAFRICA People Overview Open & User Innovation Back Open & User Innovation Projects & Awards Education Publications Overview Events Contacts News Team Events & Seminars Highlights SOCIALinNOVA-HUB ERA Chair Community Corporate Link Back Corporate Link Overview Talent Recruitment FAQ Corporate Collaboration Fundraising Back Fundraising Why donate? Our impact Get involved and meet our team Our Donors FAQ Donate Now for Scholarships Alumni Back Alumni Overview Lifelong Learning Talent Community Team Get Involved Centers, Labs & Forums Back Centers, Labs & Forums Behavioral Lab Back Behavioral Lab Overview Projects Students Instructors People Contacts Inclusive Community Forum Back Inclusive Community Forum Overview Community Employability Back Employability Overview Inclusive Journey Recruitment Peer2Peer Process Education Back Education Overview Inclusion Labs Process Empower to Employ Inclusion Projects Team Contacts Press Clipping VCW Lab Back VCW Lab Overview Projects Education Publications People Nova SBE Teaching & Innovation Center Back Nova SBE Teaching & Innovation Center About us Our offer Faculty Hub Project-Based Learning Teaching Excellence Community Impact Get Involved Institutes Back Institutes Nova SBE Haddad Entrepreneurship Institute Back Nova SBE Haddad Entrepreneurship Institute Overview Students Startups Research People What’s Happening Contacts Mentors Network Nova SBE Westmont Institute of Tourism & Hospitality Back Nova SBE Westmont Institute of Tourism & Hospitality Overview Education Global Research Societal Outreach Africa People Contacts Digital Data Design Institute Back Digital Data Design Institute Overview AI X Lab Learning Pathways Join as a partner! People Events Contacts News Nova SBE Public Policy Institute Life at Nova SBE Overview About the campus Getting started Student Support Community Engagement Well-being FAQ International Students Nova Way of Life What's Happening Newsroom Back Newsroom Overview Specialists Media Kit Contacts Press Releases News Events RRP @ Nova SBE Programs Master's in Management Overview Study Abroad Fees Careers Scholarships & Funding Apply Program Student Advising Numbers over words Nova SBE Career Services Starting a Master’s Program at Nova SBE may be one of the first steps towards a global career. Did you know that 98% of our graduates are working within six months of graduating, and that 69% of those have an international career? Supported by Nova SBE throughout their Master’s studies, graduates make their first steps into working life in a wide variety of sectors, positions, companies, and countries. Whether you already know how you plan to impact the world or whether you are still trying to decide what do after your degree, know that Nova SBE has a program that will guide you all the way through your Masters’ program. The Nova SBE Career Services team runs a comprehensive program that provides you with the necessary tools to help taking the next step more effectively from day one and transform your uncertainties into bold aspirations that can really make a difference. To help students throughout the process, the Nova SBE Career Services teams's offer includes: 86% working after 3 months 98% working after 6 months 69% with an international career Career Program The Career Program offers a comprehensive series of activities - including workshops, career events, and company networking opportunities - designed to help you build market knowledge and define your personal and professional goals. Through targeted skill development, you will be equipped to become a highly competitive candidate and a thoughtful, well-rounded professional. 1:1 Career Counselling You will deepen your knowledge about yourself and use that insight to make more informed decisions about your next steps. In 1:1 career counselling sessions, you’ll get guidance when you’re unsure and practical support to help you prepare for job interviews and navigate recruitment processes. Career Fairs Two exclusive events to meet and network with recruiters from leading international and national companies. Corporate Events By joining Corporate Events, you’ll meet employers and alumni, learn what different companies and organizations are really like, and get a better understanding of today’s job market. Career Center by JobTeaser The JobTeaser portal, from the Nova SBE Career Services team, connects students to the job market, providing access to job offers and corporate and career events. Career Mentoring Program The Career Mentoring Program is an optional service that pairs you with a Nova SBE alumni mentor, giving you access to real-world perspectives, honest guidance, and a network that goes beyond the classroom - all to support your career development and help you navigate your next steps with confidence. Online Tools To support you throughout your career journey, you will have access to a wide range of resources covering every stage of the process — from crafting a compelling CV and cover letter, to mastering networking, preparing for interviews, and navigating your job search. Our online tools, including JobTeaser, Career Set, Big Interview, Graduate First, and Case Coach, are available to help you research the market, connect with opportunities, and put your best foot forward at every step. Most Common sectors Consulting Financial Services Consumer Goods Technology Some companies that recruit at Nova SBE Accenture Amazon Bain & Company Boston Consulting Group BNP Paribas Deloitte EY L'Oréal McKinsey & Company NOS PwC Sonae Where are we To find out about all the ways the Nova SBE Career Services  team can support you and other helpful information, meet us at our office D124. Contact (+351) 213 822 792 careers@novasbe.pt Are you ready to embrace the future? Good choices can change the course of the future. Deciding what you want for your future is never easy, but Nova SBE can help you. To offer students a chance to discover where they can excel and have a meaningful career, we also share OBIPNOVA . This is a NOVA University Lisbon’s Rectory initiative that involves all NOVA schools. It aims to produce information about the career trajectory of all NOVA students regardless of their study cycle. Every year, it evaluates the professional activity of those who graduated to provide the NOVA community rigorous and reliable indicators about the career and placement of its graduates’ achievements. Learn all about OBIPNOVA here Share Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Email Contacts Contacts & Directions Ecosystem Students Alumni Research Knowledge Centers Shortcuts Join our School Regulations & P