ummer Schools PHD Summer School Executive Education Back Executive Education Homepage Open Programs Back Open Programs Marketing, Sales & Operations Sustainability & Impact Leadership & Change Management Management & Strategy Finance & Economics AI Data Digital Innovation & Entrepreneurship Companies Program Finder Calendar Faculty Contact us Blog Faculty & Research Faculty Research Areas Back Research Areas Finance Economics Management Research Unit Back Research Unit Overview Projects Publications Impact Highlights Chairs PhD Programs Reports Knowledge Centers Back Knowledge Centers Data, Operations & Technology Back Data, Operations & Technology Overview X-Collider Education Projects Publications Opportunities Team Contacts Events News Economics for Policy Economics of Education Back Economics of Education News Projects Publications Overview Events People Contacts MSc & PhD Environmental Economics Back Environmental Economics Overview Publications Events News Contacts Projects People Finance Back Finance About Us Education Finance PHD Events Projects Research People Events News Contacts Health Economics & Management Back Health Economics & Management Overview Contacts Events People News Publications Projects Leadership for Impact Back Leadership for Impact Overview People Projects Contacts Get involved Research Reports NOVAFRICA Back NOVAFRICA People Overview Open & User Innovation Back Open & User Innovation Projects & Awards Education Publications Overview Events Contacts News Team Events & Seminars Highlights SOCIALinNOVA-HUB ERA Chair Community Corporate Link Back Corporate Link Overview Talent Recruitment FAQ Corporate Collaboration Fundraising Back Fundraising Why donate? Our impact Get involved and meet our team Our Donors FAQ Donate Now for Scholarships Alumni Back Alumni Overview Lifelong Learning Talent Community Team Get Involved Centers, Labs & Forums Back Centers, Labs & Forums Behavioral Lab Back Behavioral Lab Overview Projects Students Instructors People Contacts Inclusive Community Forum Back Inclusive Community Forum Overview Community Employability Back Employability Overview Inclusive Journey Recruitment Peer2Peer Process Education Back Education Overview Inclusion Labs Process Empower to Employ Inclusion Projects Team Contacts Press Clipping VCW Lab Back VCW Lab Overview Projects Education Publications People Nova SBE Teaching & Innovation Center Back Nova SBE Teaching & Innovation Center About us Our offer Faculty Hub Project-Based Learning Teaching Excellence Community Impact Get Involved Institutes Back Institutes Nova SBE Haddad Entrepreneurship Institute Back Nova SBE Haddad Entrepreneurship Institute Overview Students Startups Research People What’s Happening Contacts Mentors Network Nova SBE Westmont Institute of Tourism & Hospitality Back Nova SBE Westmont Institute of Tourism & Hospitality Overview Education Global Research Societal Outreach Africa People Contacts Digital Data Design Institute Back Digital Data Design Institute Overview AI X Lab Learning Pathways Join as a partner! People Events Contacts News Nova SBE Public Policy Institute Life at Nova SBE Overview About the campus Getting started Student Support Community Engagement Well-being FAQ International Students Nova Way of Life What's Happening Newsroom Back Newsroom Overview Specialists Media Kit Contacts Press Releases News Events RRP @ Nova SBE Programs CEMS Master's in International Management Overview Program Apply Scholarships & Funding Fees Careers Graduate Profile International Experience CEMS Career Support Program at Nova SBE CEMS students at Nova SBE have the exclusive opportunity to receive personalized guidance to help them achieve their professional goals. Nova SBE offers five Coaching Tracks to the CEMS students: a. “Tactical Career Planning” For students who already have a job offer, or are very clear about their career plan – This track is managed by AMROP (Executive Search Firm). b. “Owning your Career Path” For students who are open to multiple career options or unsure about their plans – With the support of a dedicated professional coach. c. “Social & Enviromental Impact” For students who ambition to pursue a career dedicated to positive social and environmental impact – Alongside the Nova SBE Leadership for Impact Knowledge Center. d. “Entrepreneurship” for students who wish to develop their entrepreneurial venture or work in Venture Capital – Alongside the Nova SBE Haddad Entrepreneurship Institute. e. “Getting a Job in Consulting/Investment Banking” For students who ambition to work in top strategy consulting or investment banking – with the support of Nova SBE CEMS Alumni working in the world's most prestigious strategy consulting firms and investment banks. Additionally , students have exclusive access to the following events and platforms, in support of their job search: The Annual Career Forum – a two-day job fair comprised of skill seminars, company presentations, CV revision, a speed networking session, and pre-scheduled job interviews. An online “job market” database A Global Advisory and Mentoring Program Learn more Career Opportunities Check some numbers below: Nova SBE CEMS 2024 Graduate Profile 75% are working outside of Portugal 58% are working in Consulting 17% are working in the Financial Sector 17% are working in the FMCG (Fast-Moving Consumer Goods) sector CEMS @Nova SBE Top 5 recruiters in 2024: 1. Boston Consulting Group 2. PricewaterhouseCoopers 3. Bain & Company 4. Mastercard 5. Oliver Wyman Are you ready to embrace the future? Good choices can change the course of the future. Deciding what you want for your future is never easy, but Nova SBE can help you. To offer students a chance to discover where they can excel and have a meaningful career, we also share OBIPNOVA . This is a NOVA University Lisbon’s Rectory initiative that involves all NOVA schools. It aims to produce information about the career trajectory of all NOVA students regardless of their study cycle. Every year, it evaluates the professional activity of those who graduated to provide the NOVA community with rigorous and reliable indicators about the career and placement of its graduates’ achievements. LEARN ALL ABOUT OBIPNOVA HERE Share Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Email Contacts Contacts & Directions Ecosystem Students Alumni Research Knowledge Centers Shortcuts Join our School Regulations & Public Announcements Fundação Alfredo de Sousa Library Nova SBE Today Moodle@NovaSBE Webmail Student Hub Whistleblower Portal Follow us Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn Youtube Accredited by: Member of: Participant in: Recovery and Resilience Plan (RRP) Privacy Policy Cookies Policy Back to top"
