    "https://www.novasbe.unl.pt/Portals/0/Job%20Market/Position%20Announcement%20-%20MIS%202026%20-%202.pdf?_gl=1*1dkl70r*_up*MQ..*_ga*MTQ3NjQyMTUwOC4xNzg4Mjg5Nzc1*_ga_NRJH2682FN*czE3ODgyODk3NzMkbzEkZzAkdDE3ODgyODk3NzMkajYwJGwwJGg3NTg5MTkxNDk.": {
      "title": "Management of Information Systems Professor (open rank) at",
      "description": " \n \nManagement of Information Systems Professor (open rank) at \nNovaSBE \n \n \nPosition: Assistant, Associate Professor in Information Systems \nStarting date: September 1, 2027 \nInstitution: Nova School of Business and Economics (Universidade Nova de Lisboa) \nLocation: Lisbon, Portugal  \n \nPosition description: Nova School of Business and Economics (Nova SBE), a triple -\naccredited institution (AACSB, EQUIS , and AMBA), open s a position the Assistant  or \nAssociate (tenure track) Professor level in  Management of Information Systems  starting \non September 1, 202 7. Applicants should have a Ph.D. degree in Management of \nInformation Systems, Business Analytics, Computer Science or a related discipline by the \nstart date. Applicants should exhibit a solid research record and need to demonstrate \nability to publish in leading international business peer-reviewed journals , such as \nManagement Science , Information Systems Research,  and MIS Quarterly . Selected \napplicants are also expected to contribute to teaching in Management of Information \nSystems, Business Analytics, Data Management, Privacy,  or other related areas. \nCompensation is competitive with top universities in Europe. \nSchool description: Nova SBE offers programs in management, economics, and finance \nat the undergraduate, master, MBA, and doctorate levels, as well as executive education. \nNova SBE provides an international research environment and ranks consistently among \nthe top business schools in Europe. To support the development of a research -oriented \ncareer, Nova SBE provides a balanced teaching workload , compensation, and research-\nsupport incentives that are competitive with top business schools in Europe. English is \nthe working language of the school and knowledge of Portuguese is not a requirement.  \nNova SBE’s campus is in Lisbon at Carcavelos Beach. Lisbon is consistently ranked one of \nthe cities with the best quality of life in the world and offers an outstanding combination \nof exceptional lifestyle, relatively low cost of living, and an extensive set of cultural and \nleisure opportunities.  \nApplication details: Applications should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research \nstatement, teaching statement and job market paper. Applications will be assessed on a \nrolling basis and candidates who submit their application package by October 1, 2026 will \nbe given priority and considered for an interview during the annual INFORMS conference. \nAll applications must be received by November 15, 202 6. Applications will be accepted \nonline and must be submitted HERE (Qualtrics form). \n \nReferrers can send recommendation letters directly to faculty.affairs@novasbe.pt upon \nrequest. \n \n\n \nGeneral details about working at Nova SBE to be found:  \nJOIN OUR SCHOOL > Appointment of Professor of Management of Information Systems \n> Announcement \nAdditional information can be obtained from: \nFaculty Affairs Department (faculty.affairs@novasbe.pt) \nProf. Michail Batikas (michail.batikas@novasbe.pt) \nProf. Rodrigo Belo (rodrigo.belo@novasbe.pt) \nProf. Yufei Shen (yufei.shen@novasbe.pt) \n \nInfo-EUREXESS \nThe conditions of employment comply with the terms of Regulation no 409/2018 of 20 June, and the Labour \nCode, approved by Law no 7/2009 of 12 February, with subsequent amendments (\"Labour Code\"). Salary is \nsubject to training and experience and may vary depending on the category (Assistant, Associate or Full) and \ncareer stage and  based on a full -time contract of 35 hours. Favourable tax agreements may apply to non -\nPortuguese applicants. NovaSBE  has attractive employment conditions, which include a holiday \nand Christmas allowance and a generous number of vacation days. \n "
    },
    "https://www.novasbe.unl.pt/Portals/0/Job%20Market/Position%20Announcement%20-%20Assistant%20prof%20round%202.pdf?_gl=1*1dkl70r*_up*MQ..*_ga*MTQ3NjQyMTUwOC4xNzg4Mjg5Nzc1*_ga_NRJH2682FN*czE3ODgyODk3NzMkbzEkZzAkdDE3ODgyODk3NzMkajYwJGwwJGg3NTg5MTkxNDk.": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Organizational Behavior & Human Resources",
      "description": " \n \nAssistant Professor of Organizational Behavior & Human Resources \nManagement \nat Nova School of Business and Economics \nCarcavelos, Portugal  \n \nNova School of Business and Economics invites applications for an Assistant Professor \nresearch tenure track faculty position  in the field of Organizational Behavior & Human \nResources Management. This position is with in the Management & Organizations sub -\narea. \nPosition: 1 Assistant Professor research tenure track  positions in the field of \nOrganizational Behavior & Human Resources Management  \nStarting date: 1 September 2027 \nRequirements: Candidates should have a Ph.D. degree, or have defended their doctoral \ndissertation, in Human Resources Management, Organizational Behavior, or in a closely \nrelated field, before the start date. Candidates should demonstrate research excellence \nin the field of Human Resources  Management or Organizational Behavior . Candidates \nshould have high-quality research output commensurate with the rank for which they are \napplying. Some teaching experience is required. Preference is for candidates who have \nHRM expertise and can impart this to our students in the form of courses such as Human \nResources Analytics, Personnel Selection, Talent Management, Global Human Resources, \nHuman Resources Analytics, or other Human Resources Management-related offerings.  \nThe selected candidate will contribute to research and teaching excellence at Nova SBE.  \nApplication details:  \nApplications are to be submitted HERE by the 31st of October, 2026. They should include: \n \n• 1-page cover letter \n• Updated CV  \n• A published or working paper  representative of one’s area of expertise, topically \nand methodologically  \n• Statement of research \n• 3 referees, whom we may contact for a reference letter at a later stage \n \nApplicants successful in the first stage of recruitment will be contacted to confirm travel \narrangements for flyout visits in late November or early December of 2026. \nSchool description : Nova S chool of Business and Economics (Nova S BE) is a triple -\naccredited institution (AACSB, EQUIS and AMBA) offering programs in  management, \neconomics, and finance at the undergraduate, masters, MBA, and doctorate levels. The \n\nschool provides an international research environment and consistently ranks among the \ntop business schools in Europe.  \nTo support the development of a research -oriented career, Nova SBE  provides a very \nbalanced teaching workload , compensation competitive with other business schools in \nEurope, and research-supportive incentives. English is the working language of the school \nand knowledge of Portuguese is not a requirement.  General details about working at \nNova SBE to be found here. \nAdditional information can be obtained from: \nProfessor Marco Berti (marco.berti@novasbe.pt) \nProfessor Jenny M. Hoobler (jenny.hoobler@novasbe.pt) \nFaculty Affairs Department (faculty.affairs@novasbe.pt) \n \n \nInfo-EURAXESS \nThe conditions of employment comply with the terms of Regulation no 409/2018 of 20 June, and the Labour \nCode, approved by Law no 7/2009 of 12 February, with subsequent amendments (\"Labour Code\"). Salary is \nsubject to training and experience and may vary depending on the category (Assistant, Associate or Full) and \ncareer stage and  based on a full -time contract of 35 hours. Favourable tax agreements may apply to non -\nPortuguese applicants. Nova  SBE has attractive employment conditions, which include a holiday \nand Christmas allowance and a generous number of vacation days. \n "
    },
    "https://www.novasbe.unl.pt/Portals/0/Job%20Market/Position%20in%20Marketing%2027-28v2.pdf?_gl=1*1dkl70r*_up*MQ..*_ga*MTQ3NjQyMTUwOC4xNzg4Mjg5Nzc1*_ga_NRJH2682FN*czE3ODgyODk3NzMkbzEkZzAkdDE3ODgyODk3NzMkajYwJGwwJGg3NTg5MTkxNDk.": {
      "title": "Professor in Marketing",
      "description": "Nova SBE: Appointment of \nProfessor in Marketing \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nPhoto by IPF \n \n\n3 \n \nA community \ndedicated to the \ndevelopment \nof talent and \nknowledge that \nimpacts the world. \nAppointment \nof Professor \nin Marketing \n \n \n \nCONTENTS \n \n \nWelcome to Nova SBE - A message from the Dean | 4 \nShall we expand our horizons? - A message from our Faculty | 5 \nAppointment of Professor of Marketing | 6 \nLeading Expertise: Our Marketing Group | 8 \nA School of Business and Economics… and so, so much more | 10 \nLife at Nova: Lisbon & Cascais | 12 \n  \n4 5 \n \nWelcome to Nova SBE \nA message from the Dean \nShall we expand our horizons? \nA message from our Faculty \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nAt Nova SBE, we firmly believe in the unstoppable nature \nof change. Our world is in a constant state of \ntransformation, and it is our responsibility to adapt and \nthrive in this dynamic environment. In these challenging \ntimes, we envision our school excelling in research and \npropelling forward the internationalization process, \nensuring that Nova SBE remains at the forefront of \nacademic excellence. \n \nOur vision is rooted in the firm belief that our faculty will \ndrive the change to come. We are committed to staying \nahead of the curve, continuously engaging in \ngroundbreaking research, and fostering a culture of \ninnovation. With an exceptional faculty and a strong \nreputation, we aim to train and nurture successful \nleaders who will contribute to an open, sustainable, and \ninclusive world. \n \nFor over 40 years, Nova SBE has embraced this belief and \nhas been a beacon of excellence and innovation. Our \nfaculty members have been pioneers in their fields, \nconducting cutting-edge research and relentlessly \npursuing personal and professional development. Our \nprograms are designed to empower students, enabling \nthem to discover their true potential, cultivate the \nnecessary skills, and develop the mindset that breeds \nachievement. We are proud to see our graduates embark \non careers of personal success and societal impact. \nWhat truly sets Nova SBE apart is our supportive \ncommunity. It extends beyond our staff and faculty \nto include our esteemed alums and external \ninstitutions that share our passion for knowledge \nand talent development. Together, we have created \na nurturing environment where impactful \nknowledge is cultivated and talent is enhanced, \nmaking a difference that reverberates across the \nglobe and society at large.  \n \nAs we have done in the past, tomorrow will be a \nspace where ideas and ideals can naturally and \nsafely flourish for the public good. It will continue to \nbe the best place for young (in spirit) minds and kind \nspirits to develop and grow with boldness. Our \nunwavering commitment to providing knowledge \nand enhancing talent will remain steadfast and \nfreely shared with those who seek it. \n \nTomorrow, just like yesterday, we are open to you. \nTogether, we are dedicated to making all of this \nhappen here at Nova SBE. Join us as we shape a \nfuture that inspires, embraces change, and redefines \nexcellence in research and internationalization. \n \nPedro Oliveira \nDean of Nova SBE \nWe, Nova SBE’s faculty, are passionate professionals \nand committed lifelong learners, driven by a spirit of \ncollegiality and freedom. We truly adhere to our \nschool’s values of rigour, impact, vanguardism, \nconnectivity, and worldliness. \n \nOur school was built by bold entrepreneurs that \ndared to dream big. Their achievements proudly \ninspire us to imagine brighter futures, to resiliently \nsearch for new  knowledge, and to energize and \nempower the leaders that will transform society in \na meaningful way. \n \nIn four decades, we have grown from a small group of \neconomists to a diverse body with different \nspecializations and worldviews, determinant to set \nthe school as a proud triple crown institution ranked \namong the best in the world. \n \nWe are aware of our responsibility in our community \nand the world. Our research sets new pathways to \npolicy makers, regulators, business ecosystems, and \nsociety. All of our actions are driven by a deep ethical \ncommitment to build a sustainable future with our \nstakeholders. \nWe are recognized for our active research, presence in \npowerful global networks, and outstanding learning \njourneys deeply connected to practice. We are in a moment \nof transformation that includes more flexible employment, \ndisruptive strategy, and consolidation of internal processes. \nTo seize the opportunities brought by this moment, we will \ndrive our performance to increase excellence, impact, \ninnovation, and academic leadership. \n \nWe consciously embrace the challenging times ahead. \nThe audacious ambition of building a school for the \nfuture in a smart campus, the digital disruptions that \nchange the experience of research and learning, the \nemerging academic areas we strive to develop, the \nambiguity and uncertainty of our common future. We \nwelcome it all with hope. \n \nThe energy that drove our founders will feed our \nactions and open our minds and hearts to the world \nand the future ahead. \n \nCatia Batista \nVice Dean of Research \n\n6 7 \n \n \n \nAppointment of Professor in Marketing \n2027/2028 \n \n \n \nNova SBE seeks to appoint tenure-track faculty in \nthe Marketing Area. Appointees will be strong \nresearchers in the field of quantitative marketing, \npublishing in top journals with global impact. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nAppointees will be considered for Assistant, Associate, \nor Full professor positions . They should be willing to \nwork in a top -school with values of rigour, impact, \nvanguardism, connectivity, and worldliness. \n \nBeing open to the world is very important to us. Our \nProfessors are willing to develop their activities in an \ninternational environment that extends far beyond \nthe walls of our campus. \n \nWe are recognized by our connection to researchers \nin large networks and for worldwide impact that \nextends from Europe to Africa, the Americas, and \nAsia. We aim at this openness and reach in our \nresearch, our teaching and by engaging with \ngovernments, industries, businesses and society. \n \nWe believe that strong scholarship begins in a \nlong- term commitment to self-development and \nrequires a \ncollaborative environment in which faculty feels \nsupported in highly demanding tasks. Thus, we search \nfor high potential faculty and in addition to traditional \nresearch structures, we offer additional resources via \nour Knowledge Centers. \n \nAt Nova SBE, appointees for senior ranks are \ninternational scholars with a proven record of \nexcellence, impact, and leadership. They establish \nbold research agendas that aim to change the world \nof management and create more responsible \npractices. They often also secure grant applications \nand develop international collaborations with top \nuniversities and societal players around the world. \nRESEARCH & TEACHING \nOur faculty have the full support of the school \n(time and resources) to dedicate themselves to \nresearch and to publishing in top journals with \nacademic and societal impact. We expect faculty \nto: \n \n• Develop top impactful research, published in \nworld- leading international journals; \n• Collaborate in the Ph.D. program and Knowledge \nCenters’ projects; \n• Further expand the research networks; \n• Develop courses, deliver teaching, and supervise \ntasks for undergraduate and graduate programs. \n \nSenior appointees also: \n \n• Mentor junior faculty members; \n• Collaborate in the development of a strong \nresearch agenda for their area; \n• Raise research funding from public agencies and \nprivate sponsors; \n• Develop academic leadership by actively \nparticipating in the decision-making processes of \nthe \nschool, and develop relationships with local, \nnational, and international communities. \nACADEMY-SOCIETY ENGAGEMENT \nNova SBE promotes the active participation of senior \nfaculty in executive education, and engagement in \nknowledge co-creation with government, industries, \nfinancial systems, businesses, and society, through \nthe development of action research, specialized \nstudies, and consulting services. \n \nWe endeavour to secure endowed Chair s, to be \noffered as incentive s to senior professors \nresponsible for developing their field. Chair ed \nprofessors are  responsible for developing quality \nresearch often with interdisciplinary approach es, \nand disseminate and connect research outputs \nwith business and societal players. \nTERMS OF EMPLOYMENT \nFaculty careers are organized around a tenure system \nwith substantial probation periods that protect \nresearchers from early termination, so that they feel \nsecure to develop impactful projects with long-term \noutputs.  \n \nTenure and career progression are granted by a \ncollegial body that represents all tenured faculty \n(Scientific Council). Compensation is competitive with \ntop European schools and rewards outstanding \nresearch. \n \nSalaries are complemented with research budgets, \nvariable components, benefits, generous vacation days \n(22 working days/year) and a sabbatical leave, full paid, \nafter 6 years of full-time dedication. \n \nInternational and Portuguese faculty living abroad may \nbenefit from a lower tax rate (IRS flat rate - 20%) according \nto the Portuguese tax code. \n\n8 \n \nLeading Expertise \nThe Marketing Group \n \nTop notch research \nprojects with worldwide reach \nTeaching & Engagement \nconnected to relevant players \n \n \n \n \n  \nWe hold a regular Marketing seminar series featuring \nworldwide renowned experts on Consumer \nBehaviour and Quantitative Marketing topics.  \n \n \nOur group habitually publishes in top Marketing \njournals, including the Journal of Consumer \nResearch, Journal of Marketing Research, \nManagement Science, Marketing Science, and \nQuantitative Marketing and Economics. \n \n \nOur faculty regularly attends and presents in \nacademic conferences around the world as well as in \nresearch seminars in other academic institutions. \nOur group promotes the engagement of faculty and \nstudents with industry and practitioners. Faculty \nmembers are regularly invited to present at leading \ninternational firms. \n \n \nFaculty can supervise team-based work, with a \nproblem solving in a consultancy-like project or \nresearch approach to empirical questions. It is part \nof the academic program  of the Nova SBE Masters’ \nstudents. Examples of projects include experimental \nprojects in consumer behaviour, market research \nexercises, conjoint analysis, as well as collaborations \nwith organizations looking for solutions to real-world \nissues.\n  \n \n \n \n \nThe Marketing Faculty is recognized by its \noutstanding international performance and paves \nthe way to a deeper understanding of marketing-\nrelated topics. \n \nAll faculty have experience abroad and the vast \nmajority holds a PhD from top international \nuniversities. \n \nWe highly support the development of junior \nfaculty, through mentoring, exchanges, and \nuniversity-wide programs. All faculty is sponsored to \nattend top international conferences and \nencouraged to participate in development networks. \n \nOutstanding faculty may also apply to visit \ninternational institutions for one semester under a \nsponsored fellowship. \n \n \nKNOWLEDGE CENTERS & LABS \nNova SBE’s Knowledge Centres (KC) and Laboratories \n(LAB) are a core element of Nova SBE’s mission, as \nthey enable faculty members, staff, and partners to \nintegrate fundamental and applied research and \ncoordinate efforts towards knowledge co-creation \nand innovation in specific fields that are strategic to \nthe future of the School. \n \nKCs allow several faculty members to develop joint \nactivity towards a clear integration of different \nsteps in the knowledge development process, from \nfundamental to applied research, science outreach \nand communication, teaching, and advisory and \nconsulting services. \n \nThe Behavioural Lab provides ideal conditions in \nwhich research, experiments, and measurement are \nperformed, leading to the development of research \ndata and creative ideas, frameworks, products, and \nservices. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nRow 1 (left to right): André Trindade, Andres Montealegre, António Marinho Torres, Arash Laghaie \nRow 2 (left to right): Arnaud Monnier, Carmen Lages, Catherine da Silveira, Daniela Schmitt \nRow 3 (left to right): Fan Zhang, Irene Consiglio, Luís Lages, Luís Martinez  \nRow 4 (left to right): Natalie Truong Faust, Nicole Mead, Pedro Gardete, Sofia Kousi \nOur student -led Nova Marketing club partners \nwith enterprises, start -ups and charity \nfoundations to undertake marketing and strategy \nconsulting projects. \nThe Nova Social Consulting club offers pro-bono \nconsulting services to NGOs and Social Enterprises, \nallowing them to understand and be closer to the \nPortuguese social ecosystem. \n \nJunior faculty focus their time on research \nactivities and have access to mentoring resources \nprovided by the school. \n\n10  \nA School of Business and Economics… \nand so, so much more \ndeveloping knowledge and talent that impacts the world \nAn extended community \nconnected and open \n \n \n \nToday our faculty, students, staff, alumni, and \ncorporate partners connect in a powerful ecosystem \nin which research and innovation can truly transform \nsociety. \n \nThe researchers in our school seldom work alone. \nThey are members of international networks, travel \nregularly to present their work in leading events, \nhold positions on the editorial boards of leading \njournals, and produce multiple award-winning \npublications each year. \n \n \nOur core faculty represents more 26 nationalities \nand is regularly invited to speak at top schools \naround the world.\nAn innovation lab \nresearch in a vibrant ecosystem \n \n \n \nKnowledge and Activation Centers develop our \nacademic \nareas and offer pioneering research and innovation: \n \n• Data Science \n• Economics for Policy \n• Education \n• Environmental \n• Finance \n• Health \n• Leadership for Impact \n• Novafrica \n• Open and User Innovation \n• Value Creation Wheel \n \n \nA REFERENCE FOR EXCELLENCE \nFounded in 1978, Nova SBE is one of the leading \nbusiness schools in Europe and the most prestigious \nPortuguese school in economics, finance, and \nmanagement. \n \nOur Undergraduate, Masters, Ph.D., and MBA \nprograms are taught  in English, and we also offer \nbilingual Executive Education programs. Nova SBE’s \nvalues are: \n \nRigor.  Excellence in all School activities,  from \nstudents’ admissions  to academic analysis, research \nand School management. \n \nImpact. Commitment to transform the world in \nresponsible and inclusive ways. \n \nVanguardism.  Frontier-testing  attitude,  innovative  \nmindset  open  to  disruption. \n \nConnectivity. Responsibility for establishing bonds \nwith society and external stakeholders to engage as a \nglobal and supportive community. \n \nWorldliness. Striving to experience other cultures and \nengaging in cross-cultural synergies with an open \nattitude that enhances diversity in all its dimensions.\n \nTriple crown accreditation, universal business school \n5 palmes, and member of leading international \nalliances. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nOne of the top schools in rankings from Financial \nTimes and Eduniversal. \n \n \n2025 Financial Times Ranking Positions \n \n#17 European Business School Rankings \n#6 Master’s in Finance  \n#4 International Master’s in Management \n#9 Executive Education Custom Programs  \n#20 Open-Enrollment Programs \n \n \n \n \nTeaching activities in our school are also \ncomplemented by visiting faculty from  top  \ninternational  schools, experts from global \nconsultants and high-quality executives from our \ncorporate partners. \n \n \nWe develop worldwide talent with a universe of 40 % \nof our students being internationals representing \nmore than 60 nationalities, and over 25 student-led \nclubs that organize more than 100 events each year, \nsuch as conferences, debates, and trips. \n \n \nThe Alumni network includes over 19 000 people in 65 \ncountries, engaged with the school in events as \nspeakers, and with current students as mentors. \n \n \nOur corporate partners represent the largest \nglobal companies in the world and the smallest \nstart-ups, that use our incubator to grow. You can \ncount on our partners to develop robust \nknowledge and impactful projects. \nOur school gathers the best contents in \nmanagement sciences and organizes international \nconferences, weekly seminars, summer schools, and \nregular exchanges with international partners. \n \n \nThe Ph.D. programs engages more than 90 young \nresearchers willing to work with faculty \nin innovative projects. \n \n \nThe MSc programs engage students that develop \ntheir thesis in consulting labs with a direct \nconnection to the corporate world, supervised  by \nfaculty. \n \n \n \nSpillovers from this dynamic environment create \nopportunities for robust research with high relevance \nto business and society. \n12 13  \nLife at Nova \nAn open campus in a vibrant place that connects the \nworld \nLisbon & Cascais \nA BISI place: bright, international, smart, \ninspiring \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nWe have built a home for a growing community, with \nthe strong support from private partners. \n \nBoasting 90 000 m², the new campus stands out as an \nidyllic scenario for a research and learning \nexperience like no other. \n \nFor researchers, it hosts data labs, experimentation \nrooms, and a permanent invitation to societal players \nthat share case studies and open interviews to include \nin open science strategies. \n \nFor learners it includes 55 classrooms, 26 \namphitheaters, and a large inviting 24h open student \nhall. \n \nOur school is also a platform open to the community \nwith state of the art technology, a startup \naccelerator, an innovation lab, co -working spaces, \nan exquisite Alumni club, a modern library, a health \ncenter, a gym, a food court, stores and services to \nsupport students and faculty, and an open passage \nto the beach. \nNova SBE is a welcoming and \nsupportive community that \nembraces diversity. You will find \nhere a culture open to the world \nwith a new generation of \nchangemakers. \n \nNETWORKING: A meeting point to connect diversity in \nfruitful co-creation: international researchers, \nstudents, companies, and the broader community. \n \nCOLLABORATIVE LEARNING: The best future for human \nand machine interaction with new approaches focused \non interaction and collaborative learning. \n \nA GREAT PLACE TO LIVE: Cozy inside and sunny outside, \nit benefits from fantastic weather and inspires \neveryone with a clear horizon of endless possibility. \nOur campus connects Lisbon and Cascais, with a \nsunny window to the converging forces of a river and \nan ocean in coastal Europe. \n \nThis converging point has always been at the center \nof innovation. It inspired bold, resilient efforts to \nconnect the world, it drove innovative ventures to \nexplore the beyond, it developed strong \nmathematics and science to empower explorers \nand pioneers. It is a clear horizon of blue sky and \nwater. \n \nResearchers, innovators, and entrepreneurs feel at \nhome here. Lisbon and Cascais host a myriad of \ninternational organizations and start-ups that \ncreated a global environment of expatriated workers \nand global trotters. \n \nIn the last years, these cities have attracted \nsignificant investments in technology and \ninnovation, with a focus on organizations that \nconnect science, business, and society. \n   SAFEST CITY IN EUROPE \n \n   COMFORTABLE FOR ENGLISH SPEAKERS \n   WELCOMING FOR EXPATRIATED WORKERS \nAND FAMILIES \n \n   70% SUNNY DAYS \n   COASTAL LIFESTYLE \n   OUTDOOR ACTIVITIES \n \n   RICH HISTORY AND CULTURE OPEN TO DIVERSITY \nAND CREATIVITY \n   GATEWAY TO THE PORTUGUESE-SPEAKING WORLD \n   A CONNECTING HUB FOR EUROPE, AFRICA, \nAND THE AMERICAS \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n14  15 \nNOVA SCHOOL OF BUSINESS & ECONOMICS \n \nCampus de \nCarcavelos \nRua da \nHolanda 1, \n2775-405 \nCarcavelos \nPortugal \n \nTel: +351 21 380 1600 \n \nContact us at: faculty.affairs@novasbe.pt \nApplication Form: Link \n \n \n \n \nnovasbe.pt \n \nPhoto by IPF \n \n "
    },
    "https://www.novasbe.unl.pt/Portals/0/Job%20Market/Position%20Announcement%20-%20Marketing%202026.pdf?_gl=1*1dkl70r*_up*MQ..*_ga*MTQ3NjQyMTUwOC4xNzg4Mjg5Nzc1*_ga_NRJH2682FN*czE3ODgyODk3NzMkbzEkZzAkdDE3ODgyODk3NzMkajYwJGwwJGg3NTg5MTkxNDk.": {
      "title": "Marketing Professor (Assistant, Associate, or Full)",
      "description": " \n \nMarketing Professor (Assistant, Associate, or Full) \n at Nova School of Business and Economics \n \n \nPosition: Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Marketing (Quantitative) \nStarting date: September 1, 2027 \nInstitution: Nova School of Business and Economics (Universidade Nova de Lisboa) \nLocation: Lisbon, Portugal  \n \nPosition description: Nova School of Business and Economics (Nova SBE), a triple -\naccredited institution (AACSB, EQUIS and AMBA), announces the opening of a \nQuantitative Marketing position at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level, \neffective September 1, 2027. Applicants should hold a Ph.D. degree in Marketing, \nEconomics, or a related discipline, and a solid research record. Candidates are expected \nto publish regularly in leading international business peer-reviewed journals  and \ncontribute to teaching in the areas of Marketing, Data Analytics, or other related areas.  \nCompensation, research resources, and  teaching load are competitive with top \nuniversities in Europe. \nSchool description: Nova SBE offers programs in management, economics, and finance \nat the undergraduate, master, MBA, and doctorate levels, as well as executive education. \nThe school  provides an international research environment and consistently ranks \namong the top business schools in Europe. To support a research-oriented career, Nova \nSBE provides a very balanced teaching workload , compensation competitive with other \nbusiness schools in Europe, and research-supporting incentives. English is the working \nlanguage of the school and knowledge of Portuguese is not a requirement.  The Lisbon \narea offers an outstanding combination of relatively low cost of living, exceptional \nlifestyle, and an extensive set of cultural and leisure opportunities.  \nApplication details: Applications should include a cover letter, CV, and three research \npapers. The application deadline is September 1, 2026, and applications will be \naccepted online here. \n \nDetails to be found here \nAdditional information can be obtained from: \nFaculty Affairs Department (faculty.affairs@novasbe.pt) \nPedro Gardete (pedro.gardete@novasbe.pt) \n \n"
    },
    "https://www.novasbe.unl.pt/Portals/0/Files/Openings/Research/2021/3_%20OpenCall%2020416_2021_HumanCapital.pdf?_gl=1*1dkl70r*_up*MQ..*_ga*MTQ3NjQyMTUwOC4xNzg4Mjg5Nzc1*_ga_NRJH2682FN*czE3ODgyODk3NzMkbzEkZzAkdDE3ODgyODk3NzMkajYwJGwwJGg3NTg5MTkxNDk.": {
      "title": "2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee",
      "description": "Notice 20416/2021 \nPublished on the 28th of October 2021 \n \n \nNotice of an international public call for Doctorate hiring under the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, \n29th August \n \n1. Call identification \nThis call, for the recruitment of two Doctorates to perform research activities on the \nscientific field of Economics with a strong quantitative component, in an employment \ncontract for an indefinite period under the Portuguese Labour Code is raised, under \nthe Decree-Law no. 57/2016, 29 August, for the project “Human capital spillovers” \nwith the reference EGE-ECO/29121/2017. \n \n2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee \nof Faculdade de Economia/ Nova School of Business and Economics. \n \n3. Non admission for the reason of lack of absolute merit \nCandidates that do not obtain at least 50 points in a scale between 0 and 100 \nmeasuring the seriation criteria will not be selected for lack of absolute merit. \n \n4. Applicable Law \nDecree-Law no. 57/206, 29 August, which approves the hiring regime of Doctorates, \naiming to stimulate the scientific and technological job market in all knowledge fields \n(RJEC) \nLaw no. 57/2017, 29 August, that rules the first change of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016. \nLabor Code, approved by Law no. 7/2009, 12 February, in its current version. \n \n5. Under the article 16th of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, the authorization of the \nGovernment members responsible for the Finance and Public Administration areas is \nnot needed, namely that defined in the no. 3 of the article 7th of the LTFP, the \nprevious positive opinion of the Government members responsible for the Finance and \nPublic Administration areas, as written in the no. 5 of the article 30th of the LTFP and \nthe procedure for the recruitment of public workers on a requalification status, \nreferred to at the article no. 265 of the LTFP. \n \n6. As stated in the article 13th of the RJEC, the Call Jury has the following member \ncomposition: \n \n• Professor Paulo M. M. Rodrigues, President of the Jury \n• Professor Pedro Portugal \n• Professor Paulo Guimarães  \n \n7. The workplace is the facilities of the Faculdade de Economia/ School of Business and \nEconomics, without prejudice to any travelling justified by the job. \n \n8. The monthly salary is as defined in the no.1 of the article 15th of the Law 57/2017, 19 \nJuly, corresponding to the level 33 of the “Tabela Remuneratória Única”, approved by \nthe ordinance no. 1553-C/2008, 31 December: €2.134,73 (two thousand one hundred \nand thirty four euros and seventy three cents). \n \n9. Will be admitted to this call any Portuguese, foreign or stateless candidate with a \nDoctoral degree in Economics or similar and a scientific and professional curriculum \nadequate to the job. If the Doctoral degree was obtained in a non-Portuguese \nUniversity it must obey to the stated in the Decree-Law no. 341/20107, 12 October, \nand any needed formalities must be completed until the end of the call. \n \n10. There are special requisites to admission to this call those defined in the previous \nnumber. \n \n11.  Under the terms of the article 5th of the RJEC, the selection is done through the \nassessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates. \n \n12. The assessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates is done \nconsidering the relevance, quality and actuality of: \na) The scientific production of the last five years considered most relevant by the \ncandidate; \nb) The applied scientific activities, or practice based, developed on the last five years \nand considered by the candidate as the most impactful; \nc) The activities of extension and of knowledge dissemination developed in the last \nfive years, namely on the context of culture and scientific practice promotion \nconsidered most relevant by the candidate; \n \n13. The five years period stated in the previous number may be extended by the Jury at a \ncandidate’s request if it is based on a scientific activity interruption due to socially \nprotected reasons, namely parental leave, serious or prolonged illness and other \nsituations legally protected  \n \n14. The assessment criteria are: \n \na) On the scientific performance parameter, the publication on the field of \nEconometrics or Statistics in top peer-reviewed International journals  \nb) On the applied research parameter, the participation in research projects in the field \nof Economics or Finance. \nc) On the computing parameter, advanced knowledge of programing languages \n(example: Python, Stata, R, MATLAB) \nd) On the activities of work on projects , the assessment will be done through an \ninterview with the jury \n. \n15. The final classification system of the candidates is done in a 0 to 100 scale, according \nto the following evaluation table: \n \nCriterion Criterion \nweighting Criterion Scoring \nScientific production in the \nfields of Econometrics, \nStatistics, Economics or \nFinance \n35% \n• Demonstrated ability to publish in \njournals classified on ABS list as level 4 or \nabove – 100 \n• Demonstrated ability to publish in \njournals classified on ABS list as level 3 – \n90 \n• Demonstrated ability to publish in \njournals classified on ABS list as level 2 -\n40 \n• Demonstrated ability to publish in other \npeer reviewed journals– 10 \n• Non demonstrated ability to publish in \npeer reviewed journals – 0 \nApplied Research – \nparticipation in research \nprojects in the fields of \nEconomics or Finance \n15% \n• Participation in applied research projects \nin the fields of Economics or Finance – \n100 \n• Participation in applied research projects \nin other fields – 50 \n• No participation in applied research \nprojects - 0 \nComputing 15% \n• Knowledge of all the following computing \nlanguages: Python, Stata, R, MATLAB – \n100 \n• Knowledge of some of the computing \nlanguages: Python, Stata, R, MATLAB – 50 \n• Absence of knowledge of any of the \ncomputing languages: Python, Stata, R, \nMATLAB. \nAttitude and work project \ncompetencies 35% \n• Demonstration of the sensibility needed \nfor a good project execution, as well as \nknowledge of the project field, assessed \nin an interview with the jury. A scale from \n0 (inadequate attitude and \ncompetencies) to 100 (excellent attitude \nand competencies) will be used. \n \n16. The admitted candidate will perform at least the following activities: \na) Microeconomics data analysis; \nb) Assistance on the development, analyses and test of econometrics tools; \nc) Participation in activities related to the project objectives, namely related to \nbibliography collection and synthesis and dissemination. \nd) Eventual participation in documents resulting from the project as co-author \n \n17. The jury deliberates through nominal voting justified according to the selection criteria \nadopted and publicized. Abstention is not allowed. \n \n18. The minutes of the jury meetings must contain a brief description of the issues \ndiscussed, as well as each member’s votes with justification, and candidates are \nentitled to read it if required. \n \n19. After the application of the selection criteria, the jury must elaborate the ranked list of \ncandidates with the respective classification. \n \n20. The final deliberation of the jury must be homologated by the Head of the Institution \nwho also decides on the hiring. \n \n21. Applications: \n21.1. Applications are formalized through an application form available to download \nat the Nova School of Business and Economics webpage - \nhttps://www2.novasbe.unl.pt/en/about-us/join-our-school -, addressed to the \nSchool’s Dean, containing the identification of the present Call, complete \ncandidate name, names of father and mother, number and date of the \nidentification document, fiscal number, date and place of birth, marital status, \noccupation, residency data and contact data, including e-mail address and phone \nnumber. \n21.2. The candidate should also attach documents that make proof of the conditions \nstated in articles 11 and 13, namely: \na) Copy of the certificate or Diploma \nb) PhD Thesis \nc) Detailed curriculum vitae, structured in accordance with items from article 14 \nd) Other relevant documents  \n \n22. The candidates should present their application forms as well as the other documents \nrequested preferably in digital versions, PDF, to the e-mail address: \nresearchposition@novasbe.pt, personally at the Faculty Affairs Department of the \nNova School of Business and Economics (“Serviço de Apoio ao Docente”), Rua da \nHolanda, nº 1, 2775-405 Carcavelos, during working hours or by post to the same \naddress. The applications sent by post must be registered with reception proving, until \nthe last day of the call opening, which is 20 working days after the publishing of the \nCall at the Diário da República. \n \n23. Candidates that do not dully formalize their applications or that do not make proof of \nthe Call requisites will be excluded. The jury can require of any candidate any \ndocument that makes proof of any declaration on the application. \n \n24. False declarations should be punished according to the law. \n \n25. The list of the accepted and excluded candidates as well as the list with the final \nclassification must be posted in the School’s facilities, at Rua da Holanda, nº 1, 2775-\n405 Carcavelos, at the Universidade Nova de Lisboa and the School’s webpages, and \nthe candidates must be notified through e-mail with Delivery Report request. \n \n26. Previous audience and deadline for final decision: As stated in the article no. 121 of \nthe Administrative Proceedings Code (“Código do Procedimento Administrativo”), \nafter being notified the candidates have 10 working days to reply. The final decision of \nthe jury must be taken during the 10 days after the deadline for applications. \n \n27. The current call is exclusively dedicated to fill the job position above mentioned and \ncan be terminated until the homologation of the candidates final ranked list. It will \nexpire at the moment that the job position is filled with the selected candidate. \n \n28. Nondiscrimination and equal access policy: Universidade Nova de Lisboa actively \npromotes a nondiscrimination and equal access policy, under which, no candidate shall \nbe prejudiced either favorable or unfavorable, deprived of any right or exempt from \nany duty, for reasons of, namely, descent, age, gender, sexual orientation, race, \nmarital status, family or economic circumstances, education, origin or social condition, \ngenetic heritage, reduced capacity for work, disability, chronic illness, nationality, \nethnicity or race, territory of origin, language, religion, political or ideological \nconvictions and union membership. \n29. In accordance with D.L. nº 29/2001, of 3 of February, candidates with disabilities are \npreferred in case of equal classification, which prevails over any other legal \npreferences. The candidates must provide a declaration of honor with the respective \ndegree of incapacity, type of disability, and the communication/expression media to \nbe used in the selection process, under the legislation mentioned above. \n "
    },
    "https://www.novasbe.unl.pt/Portals/0/Files/Openings/Research/2021/3_%20OpenCall%2020417_2021_UH.pdf?_gl=1*1dkl70r*_up*MQ..*_ga*MTQ3NjQyMTUwOC4xNzg4Mjg5Nzc1*_ga_NRJH2682FN*czE3ODgyODk3NzMkbzEkZzAkdDE3ODgyODk3NzMkajYwJGwwJGg3NTg5MTkxNDk.": {
      "title": "2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee",
      "description": "Notice 20417/2021 \nPublished on the 28th of October 2021 \n \n \nNotice of an international public call for Doctorate hiring under the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, \n29th August \n \n1. Call identification \nThis call, for the recruitment of two Doctorates to perform research activities on the \nscientific field of Computational Sciences, Data Science and Artificial Intelligence \napplied to health, in an employment contract for an indefinite period under the \nPortuguese Labour Code is raised, under the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, 29 August, for \nthe project “Identifying and Predicting Emergency Admissions” with the reference \nDSAIPA/AI/0087/2018. \n \n2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee \nof Faculdade de Economia/ Nova School of Business and Economics. \n \n3. Non admission for the reason of lack of absolute merit \nCandidates that do not obtain at least 50 points in a scale between 0 and 100 \nmeasuring the seriation criteria will not be selected for lack of absolute merit. \n \n4. Applicable Law \nDecree-Law no. 57/206, 29 August, which approves the hiring regime of Doctorates, \naiming to stimulate the scientific and technological job market in all knowledge fields \n(RJEC) \nLaw no. 57/2017, 29 August, that rules the first change of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016. \nLabor Code, approved by Law no. 7/2009, 12 February, in its current version. \n \n5. Under the article 16th of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, the authorization of the \nGovernment members responsible for the Finance and Public Administration areas is \nnot needed, namely that defined in the no. 3 of the article 7th of the LTFP, the \nprevious positive opinion of the Government members responsible for the Finance and \nPublic Administration areas, as written in the no. 5 of the article 30th of the LTFP and \nthe procedure for the recruitment of public workers on a requalification status, \nreferred to at the article no. 265 of the LTFP. \n \n6. As stated in the article 13th of the RJEC, the Call Jury has the following member \ncomposition: \n \n• Professor Joana Gonçalves de Sá, President of the Jury \n• Professor Cláudia Soares \n• Lília Perfeito, PhD \n \n7. The workplace is the facilities of the Faculdade de Economia/ School of Business and \nEconomics and the Lab of Instrumentação e Física  Experimental de Partículas (LIP), \nwithout prejudice to any travelling justified by the job. \n \n8. The monthly salary is as defined in the no.1 of the article 15th of the Law 57/2017, 19 \nJuly, corresponding to the level 33 of the “Tabela Remuneratória Única”, approved by \nthe ordinance no. 1553-C/2008, 31 December: €2.134,73 (two thousand one hundred \nand thirty four euros and seventy three cents). \n \n9. Will be admitted to this call any Portuguese, foreign or stateless candidate with a \nDoctoral degree in Economics or similar and a scientific and professional curriculum \nadequate to the job. If the Doctoral degree was obtained in a non-Portuguese \nUniversity it must obey to the stated in the Decree-Law no. 341/20107, 12 October, \nand any needed formalities must be completed until the end of the call. \n \n10. There are special requisites to admission to this call those defined in the previous \nnumber. \n \n11.  Under the terms of the article 5th of the RJEC, the selection is done through the \nassessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates. \n \n12. The assessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates is done \nconsidering the relevance, quality and actuality of: \na) The scientific production of the last five years considered most relevant by the \ncandidate; \nb) The applied scientific activities, or practice based, developed on the last five years \nand considered by the candidate as the most impactful; \nc) The skills on the use of different software’s and programming languages as \nidentified below; \nd) The activities of extension and of knowledge dissemination developed in the last \nfive years, namely on the context of culture and scientific practice promotion \nconsidered most relevant by the candidate; \n \n13. The five years period stated in the previous number may be extended by the Jury at a \ncandidate’s request if it is based on a scientific activity interruption due to socially \nprotected reasons, namely parental leave, serious or prolonged illness and other \nsituations legally protected  \n \n14. The assessment criteria are: \n \na) On the scientific performance parameter, the publication  or presentations  on \ninternational conferences that display knowledge in the areas of Biomedicine, \nComputing and Data Science, or Artificial Intelligence; \nb) On the applied research parameter, the participation in research projects that \ndisplay knowledge in the areas of Biome dicine, Computation and Data Science, or \nArtificial Intelligence, particularly in the field of health data; \nc) On the computing parameter, advanced knowledge of programing languages such \nas Python and SQL, and experience on health data management; \nd) On the activities of work on projects and skill competency, particularly what regards \ndomain of the English and Portuguese languages, as well as experience on \nteamwork and project management, the assessment will be done through the \nevaluation of the applic ation package documentation, candidate’s experience on \nnational and international projects and teams. \n. \n15. The final classification system of the candidates is done in a 0 to 100 scale, according \nto the following evaluation table: \n \nCriterion Criterion \nweighting Criterion Scoring \nScientific production that \nthat displays knowledge in \nthe areas of Biomedicine, \nComputing and Data Science, \nor Artificial Intelligence \n20% \n• At least two publications (including final \nstage of preparation) or presentations in \ninternational conferences in the areas of \nBiomedicine, Biology or Health with a \nstrong computing component or data \nscience – 100 \n• One publication or presentation as \ndescribed above – 50 \n• No publications or presentations - 0 \nApplied Research that that \ndisplays knowledge in the \nareas of Biomedicine, \nComputing and Data Science, \nor Artificial Intelligence \n30% \n• Participation in applied research projects \nin the areas of Biomedicine, Biology or \nHealth with a strong computing \ncomponent or data science – 100 \n• No Participation in applied research \nprojects in the described fields – 0 \nComputing knowledge 20% \n• Knowledge of all the following computing \nlanguages: Python and SQL (intermediate \nlevel) – 100 \n• Knowledge of one of the languages \n(intermediate level)– 50 \n• Absence of knowledge of the languages - \n0 \nAttitude and work project \ncompetencies 30% \n• Demonstration of the sensibility needed \nfor a good project execution, as well as \nknowledge of the project field. A scale \nfrom 0 (inadequate competencies) to 100 \n(excellent competencies) will be used. \n \n16. The admitted candidate will perform at least the following activities: \na) Analysis and development of data bases with medical and non-medical \ninformation relevant for the project; \nb) Management, validation, and treatment of data for the development of forecast \ninflows in real time; \nc) Participation and promotion of activities related to the project with colleagues and \nresearcher groups; \nd) Participation in activities related to the project objectives, namely related to \nbibliography collection and synthesis and dissemination, such as preparation of \nscientific papers and conference’s presentations, seminars, workshops (and \nothers) as well as organization of such project events. \n \n17. The jury deliberates through nominal voting justified according to the selection criteria \nadopted and publicized. Abstention is not allowed. \n \n18. The minutes of the jury meetings must contain a brief description of the issues \ndiscussed, as well as each member’s votes with justification, and candidates are \nentitled to read it if required. \n \n19. After the application of the selection criteria, the jury must elaborate the ranked list of \ncandidates with the respective classification. \n \n20. The final deliberation of the jury must be homologated by the Head of the Institution \nwho also decides on the hiring. \n \n21. Applications: \n21.1. Applications are formalized through an application form available to download \nat the Nova School of Business and Economics webpage - \nhttps://www2.novasbe.unl.pt/en/about-us/join-our-school -, addressed to the \nSchool’s Dean, containing the identification of the present Call, complete \ncandidate name, names of father and mother, number and date of the \nidentification document, fiscal number, date and place of birth, marital status, \noccupation, residency data and contact data, including e-mail address and phone \nnumber. \n21.2. The candidate should also attach documents that make proof of the conditions \nstated in articles 11 and 13, namely: \na) Copy of the certificate or Diploma \nb) Detailed curriculum vitae, structured in accordance with items from article \n14, in English \nc) Cover Letter, in English \nd) Contact of two references \ne) Other relevant documents  \n \n22. The candidates should present their application forms as well as the other documents \nrequested preferably in digital versions, PDF, to the e-mail address: \nresearchposition@novasbe.pt, personally at the Faculty Affairs Department of the \nNova School of Business and Economics (“Serviço de Apoio ao Docente”), Rua da \nHolanda, nº 1, 2775-405 Carcavelos, during working hours or by post to the same \naddress. The applications sent by post must be registered with reception proving, until \nthe last day of the call opening, which is 06 working days after the publishing of the \nCall at the Diário da República. \n \n23. Candidates that do not dully formalize their applications or that do not make proof of \nthe Call requisites will be excluded. The jury can require of any candidate any \ndocument that makes proof of any declaration on the application. \n \n24. False declarations should be punished according to the law. \n \n25. The list of the accepted and excluded candidates as well as the list with the final \nclassification must be posted in the School’s facilities, at Rua da Holanda, nº 1, 2775-\n405 Carcavelos, at the Universidade Nova de Lisboa and the School’s webpages, and \nthe candidates must be notified through e-mail with Delivery Report request. \n \n26. Previous audience and deadline for final decision: As stated in the article no. 121 of \nthe Administrative Proceedings Code (“Código do Procedimento Administrativo”), \nafter being notified the candidates have 10 working days to reply. The final decision of \nthe jury must be taken during the 10 days after the deadline for applications. \n \n27. The current call is exclusively dedicated to fill the job position above mentioned and \ncan be terminated until the homologation of the candidates final ranked list. It will \nexpire at the moment that the job position is filled with the selected candidate. \n \n28. Nondiscrimination and equal access policy: Universidade Nova de Lisboa actively \npromotes a nondiscrimination and equal access policy, under which, no candidate shall \nbe prejudiced either favorable or unfavorable, deprived of any right or exempt from \nany duty, for reasons of, namely, descent, age, gender, sexual orientation, race, \nmarital status, family or economic circumstances, education, origin or social condition, \ngenetic heritage, reduced capacity for work, disability, chronic illness, nationality, \nethnicity or race, territory of origin, language, religion, political or ideological \nconvictions and union membership. \n29. In accordance with D.L. nº 29/2001, of 3 of February, candidates with disabilities are \npreferred in case of equal classification, which prevails over any other legal \npreferences. The candidates must provide a declaration of honor with the respective \ndegree of incapacity, type of disability, and the communication/expression media to \nbe used in the selection process, under the legislation mentioned above. \n "
    },
    "https://www.novasbe.unl.pt/Portals/0/Files/Openings/Faculty/2_%20OpenCall_LANDUSE_ENG.pdf?_gl=1*1dkl70r*_up*MQ..*_ga*MTQ3NjQyMTUwOC4xNzg4Mjg5Nzc1*_ga_NRJH2682FN*czE3ODgyODk3NzMkbzEkZzAkdDE3ODgyODk3NzMkajYwJGwwJGg3NTg5MTkxNDk.": {
      "title": "2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee",
      "description": "Notice 17654/2021 \n Published on the 17th of September 2021 \n \n \nNotice of an international public call for Doctorate hiring under the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, \n29th August \n \n1. Call identification \nThis call, for the recruitment of two Doctorates to perform research activities on the \nscientific field of Economics and/or Environmental Sciences, in an employment contract \nfor an indefinite period under the Portuguese Labour Code is raised, under the Decree-\nLaw no. 57/2016, 29  August, for the project “Land Use Changes at The Urban -Rural \nInterface: A Portuguese Case Study ” with the reference Projeto de IC&DT – AAC n.º \n02/SAICT/2017. \n \n2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee \nof Faculdade de Economia/ Nova School of Business and Economics. \n \n3. Non admission for the reason of lack of absolute merit \nCandidates that do not obtain at least 50 points in a scale between 0 and 100 measuring \nthe seriation criteria will not be selected for lack of absolute merit. \n \n4. Applicable Law \nDecree-Law no. 57/206, 29 August, which approves the hiring regime of Doctorate s, \naiming to stimulate the scientific and technological job market in all knowledge fields \n(RJEC) \nLaw no. 57/2017, 29 August, that rules the first change of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016. \nLabor Code, approved by Law no. 7/2009, 12 February, in its current version. \n \n5. Under the article 16th of the Decree -Law no. 57/2016, the authorization of the \nGovernment members responsible for the Finance and Public Administration areas is \nnot needed, namely that defined in the no. 3 of the article 7th of the LTFP, the previous \npositive opinion of the Government members responsible for the Finance and Public \nAdministration areas, as written in the no. 5 of the article 30th of the LTFP and the \nprocedure for the recruitment of public workers on a requalification status, referred to \nat the article no. 265 of the LTFP. \n \n6. As stated in the article 13 th of the RJEC, the Call Jury has the following member \ncomposition: \n \n• Professor Maria Antonieta Cunha e Sá \n• Professor Sofia F. Franco \n• Professor Renato Rosa \n• Doctorate Carina Silva \n \n \n7. The workplace is the facilities of the Faculdade de Economia/ School of Business and \nEconomics, without prejudice to any travelling justified by the job. \n \n8. The monthly salary is as defined in the no.1 of the article 15 th of the Law 57/2017, 19 \nJuly, corresponding to the level 33 of the “Tabela Remuneratória Única”, approved by \nthe ordinance no. 1553 -C/2008, 31 December: €2.134,73 (two thousand one hundred \nand thirty four euros and seventy three cents). \n \n9. Will be admitted to this call any Portuguese, foreign or stateless candidate with a \nDoctoral degree in Economics or similar and a n adequate scientific and professional \ncurriculum. If the Doctoral degree was obtained in a non-Portuguese University it must \nobey to the stated in the Decree -Law no. 341/20107, 12 October, and any needed \nformalities must be completed until the end of the call. \n \n10. There are special requisites to admission to this call those defined in the previous \nnumber. \n \n11.  Under the terms of the ar ticle 5 th of the RJEC, the selection is done through the \nassessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates. \n \n12. The assessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates is done \nconsidering the relevance, quality and actuality of: \na) The scientific production of the last five years considered most relevant by the \ncandidate; \nb) The applied scientific activities, or practice based, developed on the last five years e \nconsidered by the candidate as the most impactful; \nc) The competencies of using different software below mentioned \nd) The activities of extension and of knowledge disseminat ion developed in the last \nfive years, namely on the context of culture and scientific practice promotion \nconsidered most relevant by the candidate; \n \n13. The five years period stated in the previous number may be extended by the Jury at a \ncandidate’s request if  it is based on a scientific activity interruption due to socially \nprotected reasons, namely parental leave, serious or prolonged illness and other \nsituations legally protected  \n \n14. The assessment criteria are: \n \na) On the scientific performance parameter, the pu blication in Economics and/or \nEnvironmental Sciences fields in top peer-reviewed International journals; \n \nb) On the applied research parameter, the participation in research projects in the \nEconomics and/or Environmental Sciences fields; \n \nc) On the computational parameter, preference for candidates with  knowledge of \nprograming language s and statistical analysis such as Stata, R, SPSS , as well as  \nArcGIS, QGIS, or other \n \nd) On the activities of work on projects, the assessment will be done through an \ninterview with the jury , mainly the fluency in English (writing and conversation), \ncommunication and interpersonal relationship competences , as well as teamwork \nand project management experience. \n  \n \n15. The final classification system of the candidates is done in a 0 to 100 scale, according to \nthe following evaluation table: \n \nCriterion Criterion \nweighting Criterion Scoring \nScientific production that \nreveals knowledge in the \nEconomics and/or \nEnvironmental Sciences \nfields \n10% \n• 10 or more publications in scientific \njournals classified on the ABS, ISI or \nSCOPUS lists - 100 \n• 5 or more publications in scientific \njournals classified on the ABS, ISI or \nSCOPUS lists - 90 \n• Less than 5 publications in scientific peer \nreviewed journals not classified on the \nABS, ISI or SCOPUS lists - 70 \n• Publications in scientific journals not \nclassified on the ABS, ISI or SCOPUS lists – \n50 \n• Non demonstrated ability to publish in \npeer reviewed journals – 0 \nApplied Research – \nparticipation in research \nprojects in the Economics \nand/or Environmental \nSciences fields \n15% \n• Participation in applied research projects \nin the Environmental Economics field– \n100 \n• Participation in applied research projects \nin the Economics field – 80 \n• Participation in applied research projects \nthat reveal knowledges in the \nenvironmental sciences - 60 \n• No participation in applied research \nprojects in the Environmental and Natural \nResources Economics field - 0 \nSoftware using experience I 15% \n• Knowledge of at least 2 of the following \ncomputing languages: Stata, R, SPSS – \n100 \n• Knowledge of only one of the following \ncomputing languages: Stata, R, SPSS – 70 \n• Knowledge of Stata (only) – 50 \n• Absence of knowledge of the computing \nlanguages: Stata, R, SPSS - 0 \nSoftware using experience II 15% \n• Experience using software like ArcGIS, \nQGIS, among other – 70 \n• Absence of experience using software like \nArcGIS, QGIS, among other - 30 \nAttitude and work project \ncompetencies 45% \nDemonstration of the sensibility needed for a \ngood project execution, as well as knowledge \nof the project field, assessed in an interview \nwith the jury. A scale from 0 (inadequate \nattitude and competencies) to 100 (excellent \nattitude and competencies) will be used. \n \n16. The admitted candidate will perform at least the following activities: \na) Development and implementation of statistical techniques using the appropriate \nsoftware such as Stata and/or R or SPSS; \nb) Microeconomic data mapping using geographical information systems (e.g. ArcGIS, \nQGIS or similar) \nc) Participation and promotion of activities within the project scope with other \ncolleagues and research groups. \nd) Participation in activities related to the project aims, namely those related to the \ncollecting and synthesis of bibliographic data and dissemination activities such as \nscientific papers preparation, presentations in conferences, seminars, workshops, \netc., as well as the organization of such events within the scope of the project. \n \n17. The jury deliberates through nominal voting justified according to the selection criteria \nadopted and publicized. Abstention is not allowed. \n \n18. The minutes of the jury meetings must contain a brief description of the issues \ndiscussed, as well as each member’s votes with justification, and candidates are entitled \nto read it if required. \n \n19. After the application of the selection criteria, the jury must elaborate the ranked list of \ncandidates with the respective classification. \n \n20. The final deliberation of t he jury must be homologated by the Head of the Institution \nwho also decides on the hiring. \n \n21. Applications: \n21.1. Applications are formalized through an application form available to download \nat the Nova School of Business and Economics webpage  - \nhttps://www2.novasbe.unl.pt/en/about-us/join-our-school , addressed to the \nSchool’s Dean, containing the identification of the present Call, complete candidate \nname, names of father and mother, number and date of the identification \ndocument, fiscal number, date and place of birth, marital status, occupation, \nresidency data and contact data, including e-mail address and phone number. \n21.2. The candidate should also attach documents that make proof of the conditions \nstated in articles 10 and 12, namely: \na) Copy of the certificate or Diploma \nb) PhD Thesis \nc) Detailed curriculum vitae, structured in accordance with items from article 14 \nd) Other relevant documents  \n \n22. The candidates should present their application forms as well as the other documents \nrequested preferably in digital versions, PDF, to the e -mail address: \nresearchposition@novasbe.pt, personally at the Faculty Affairs Department of the Nova \nSchool of Business and Economics (“Serviço de Apoio ao Docente”), Rua da Holanda, nº \n1, 2775 -405 Carcavelos , during working hours or by post to the same address. The \napplications sent by post must be registered with reception proving,  until the last day \nof the call opening, which is 20 working days after the publishing of the Call at the Diário \nda República. \n \n23. Candidates that do not dully formalize their applications or that do not make proof of \nthe Call requisites will be excluded. The jury is allowed to require of any candidate any \ndocument that makes proof of any declaration on the application. \n \n24. False declarations should be punished according to the law. \n \n25. The list of the accepted and excluded candidates as well as the list with the final \nclassification must be posted in the School’s facilities, at Rua da Holanda, nº 1, 2775-405 \nCarcavelos, at the Universidade Nova de Lisboa and the School’s webpages, and th e \ncandidates must be notified through e-mail with Delivery Report request. \n \n26. Previous audience and deadline for final decision: As stated in the article no. 121 of the \nAdministrative Proceedings Code (“Código do Procedimento Administrativo”), after \nbeing notified the candidates have 10 working days to reply. The final decision of the \njury must be taken during the 10 days after the deadline for applications. \n \n27. The current call is exclusively dedicated to fill the job position above mentioned and can \nbe terminated until the homologation of the candidates final ranked list. It will expire at \nthe moment that the job position is filled with the selected candidate. \n \n28. Nondiscrimination and equal access policy: Universidade N ova de Lisboa actively \npromotes a nondiscrimination and equal access policy, under which, no candidate shall \nbe prejudiced either favorable or unfavorable, deprived of any right or exempt from any \nduty, for reasons of, namely, descent, age, gender, sexual orientation, race, marital \nstatus, family or economic circumstances, education, origin or social condition, genetic \nheritage, reduced capacity for work, disability, chronic illness, nationality, ethnicity or \nrace, territory of origin, language, religion, political or ideological convictions and union \nmembership. \n29. In accordance with D.L. nº 29/2001, of 3 of February, candidates with disabilities are \npreferred in case of equal classification, which prevails over any other legal preferences. \nThe candidates must provide a declaration of honor with the respective degree of \nincapacity, type of disability, and the communication/expression media to be used in \nthe selection process, under the legislation mentioned above. \n \n \n "
