    "https://www.novasbe.unl.pt/Portals/0/Files/Openings/Research/CALL%20FOR%20DOCTORATE%20HIRING%208009_2019.pdf?_gl=1*1dkl70r*_up*MQ..*_ga*MTQ3NjQyMTUwOC4xNzg4Mjg5Nzc1*_ga_NRJH2682FN*czE3ODgyODk3NzMkbzEkZzAkdDE3ODgyODk3NzMkajYwJGwwJGg3NTg5MTkxNDk.": {
      "title": "2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee",
      "description": "Notice 8009/2019 \n \n \nNotice of an international public call for Doctorate hiring under the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, \n29th August \n \n1. Call identification \nThis call, for the recruitment of a Doctorate to perform research activities on the \nscientific field of Economics with a strong quantitative component, in an employment \ncontract for an indefinite period under the Portuguese Labour Code is raised, under \nthe Decree-Law no. 57/2016, 29 August, for the project “Human capital spillovers” \nwith the reference EGE-ECO/29121/2017. \n \n2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee \nof Faculdade de Economia/ Nova School of Business and Economics. \n \n3. Non admission for the reason of lack of absolute merit \nCandidates that do not obtain at least 50 points in a scale between 0 and 100 \nmeasuring the seriation criteria will not be selected for lack of absolute merit. \n \n4. Applicable Law \nDecree-Law no. 57/206, 29 August, which approves the hiring regime of Doctorates, \naiming to stimulate the scientific and technological job market in all knowledge fields \n(RJEC) \nLaw no. 57/2017, 29 August, that rules the first change of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016. \nLabor Code, approved by Law no. 7/2009, 12 February, in its current version. \n \n5. Under the article 16th of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, the authorization of the \nGovernment members responsible for the Finance and Public Administration areas is \nnot needed, namely that defined in the no. 3 of the article 7th of the LTFP, the \nprevious positive opinion of the Government members responsible for the Finance and \nPublic Administration areas, as written in the no. 5 of the article 30th of the LTFP and \nthe procedure for the recruitment of public workers on a requalification status, \nreferred to at the article no. 265 of the LTFP. \n \n6. As stated in the article 13th of the RJEC, the Call Jury has the following member \ncomposition: \n \n• Professor Paulo M. M. Rodrigues, President of the Jury \n• Professor Pedro Portugal \n• Professor Paulo Guimarães  \n \n7. The workplace is the facilities of the Faculdade de Economia/ School of Business and \nEconomics, without prejudice to any travelling justified by the job. \n \n8. The monthly salary is as defined in the no.1 of the article 15th of the Law 57/2017, 19 \nJuly, corresponding to the level 33 of the “Tabela Remuneratória Única”, approved by \nthe ordinance no. 1553-C/2008, 31 December: €2.128,34 (two thousand one hundred \nand twenty eight euros and thirty four cents). \n \n9. Will be admitted to this call any Portuguese, foreign or stateless candidate with a \nDoctoral degree in Economics or similar and a scientific and professional curriculum \nadequate to the job. If the Doctoral degree was obtained in a non-Portuguese \nUniversity it must obey to the stated in the Decree-Law no. 341/20107, 12 October, \nand any needed formalities must be completed until the end of the call. \n \n10. There are special requisites to admission to this call those defined in the previous \nnumber. \n \n11.  Under the terms of the article 5th of the RJEC, the selection is done through the \nassessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates. \n \n12. The assessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates is done \nconsidering the relevance, quality and actuality of: \na) The scientific production of the last five years considered most relevant by the \ncandidate; \nb) The applied scientific activities, or practice based, developed on the last five years \nand considered by the candidate as the most impactful; \nc) The activities of extension and of knowledge dissemination developed in the last \nfive years, namely on the context of culture and scientific practice promotion \nconsidered most relevant by the candidate; \n \n13. The five years period stated in the previous number may be extended by the Jury at a \ncandidate’s request if it is based on a scientific activity interruption due to socially \nprotected reasons, namely parental leave, serious or prolonged illness and other \nsituations legally protected  \n \n14. The assessment criteria are: \n \na) On the scientific performance parameter, the publication on the field of \nEconometrics or Statistics in top peer-reviewed International journals  \nb) On the applied research parameter, the participation in research projects in the field \nof Economics or Finance. \nc) On the computing parameter, a dvanced knowledge of programing languages \n(example: Python, Stata, R, MATLAB) \nd) On the activities of work on projects, the assessment will be done through an \ninterview with the jury \n. \n15. The final classification system of the candidates is done in a 0 to 100 scale, according \nto the following evaluation table: \n \nCriterion Criterion \nweighting Criterion Scoring \nScientific production in the \nfields of Econometrics, \nStatistics, Economics or \nFinance \n35% \n• Demonstrated ability to publish in \njournals classified on ABS list as level 4 or \nabove – 100 \n• Demonstrated ability to publish in \njournals classified on ABS list as level 3 – \n90 \n• Demonstrated ability to publish in \njournals classified on ABS list as level 2 -\n40 \n• Demonstrated ability to publish in other \npeer reviewed journals– 10 \n• Non demonstrated ability to publish in \npeer reviewed journals – 0 \nApplied Research – \nparticipation in research \nprojects in the fields of \nEconomics or Finance \n15% \n• Participation in applied research projects \nin the fields of Economics or Finance – \n100 \n• Participation in applied research projects \nin other fields – 50 \n• No participation in applied research \nprojects - 0 \nComputing 15% \n• Knowledge of all the following computing \nlanguages: Python, Stata, R, MATLAB – \n100 \n• Knowledge of some of the computing \nlanguages: Python, Stata, R, MATLAB – 50 \n• Absence of knowledge of any of the \ncomputing languages: Python, Stata, R, \nMATLAB. \nAttitude and work project \ncompetencies 35% \n• Demonstration of the sensibility needed \nfor a good project execution, as well as \nknowledge of the project field, assessed \nin an interview with the jury. A scale from \n0 (inadequate attitude and \ncompetencies) to 100 (excellent attitude \nand competencies) will be used. \n \n16. The admitted candidate will perform at least the following activities: \na) Microeconomics data analysis; \nb) Assistance on the development, analyses and test of econometrics tools; \nc) Participation in activities related to the project objectives, namely related to \nbibliography collection and synthesis and dissemination. \nd) Eventual participation in documents resulting from the project as co-author \n \n17. The jury deliberates through nominal voting justified according to the selection criteria \nadopted and publicized. Abstention is not allowed. \n \n18. The minutes of the jury meetings must contain a brief description of the issues \ndiscussed, as well as each member’s votes with justification, and candidates are \nentitled to read it if required. \n \n19. After the application of the selection criteria, the jury must elaborate the ranked list of \ncandidates with the respective classification. \n \n20. The final deliberation of the jury must be homologated by the Head of the Institution \nwho also decides on the hiring. \n \n21. Applications: \n21.1. Applications are formalized through an application form available to download \nat the Nova School of Business and Economics webpage - \nhttps://www2.novasbe.unl.pt/en/about-us/join-our-school -, addressed to the \nSchool’s Dean, containing the identification of the present Call, complete \ncandidate name, names of father and mother, number and date of the \nidentification document, fiscal number, date and place of birth, marital status, \noccupation, residency data and contact data, including e-mail address and phone \nnumber. \n21.2. The candidate should also attach documents that make proof of the conditions \nstated in articles 11 and 13, namely: \na) Copy of the certificate or Diploma \nb) PhD Thesis \nc) Detailed curriculum vitae, structured in accordance with items from article 14 \nd) Other relevant documents  \n \n22. The candidates should present their application forms as well as the other documents \nrequested preferably in digital versions, PDF, to the e-mail address: \nresearchposition@novasbe.pt, personally at the Faculty Affairs Department of the \nNova School of Business and Economics (“Serviço de Apoio ao Docente”), Rua da \nHolanda, nº 1, 2775-405 Carcavelos, during working hours or by post to the same \naddress. The applications sent by post must be registered with reception proving, until \nthe last day of the call opening, which is 6 working days after the publishing of the Call \nat the Diário da República, that is 17 May 2019. \n \n23. Candidates that do not dully formalize their applications or that do not make proof of \nthe Call requisites will be excluded. The jury is allowed to require of any candidate any \ndocument that makes proof of any declaration on the application. \n \n24. False declarations should be punished according to the law. \n \n25. The list of the accepted and excluded candidates as well as the list with the final \nclassification must be posted in the School’s facilities, at Rua da Holanda, nº 1, 2775-\n405 Carcavelos, at the Universidade Nova de Lisboa and the School’s webpages, and \nthe candidates must be notified through e-mail with Delivery Report request. \n \n26. Previous audience and deadline for final decision: As stated in the article no. 121 of \nthe Administrative Proceedings Code (“Código do Procedimento Administrativo”), \nafter being notified the candidates have 10 working days to reply. The final decision of \nthe jury must be taken during the 10 days after the deadline for applications. \n \n27. The current call is exclusively dedicated to fill the job position above mentioned and \ncan be terminated until the homologation of the candidates final ranked list. It will \nexpire at the moment that the job position is filled with the selected candidate. \n \n28. Nondiscrimination and equal access policy: Universidade Nova de Lisboa actively \npromotes a nondiscrimination and equal access policy, under which, no candidate shall \nbe prejudiced either favorable or unfavorable, deprived of any right or exempt from \nany duty, for reasons of, namely, descent, age, gender, sexual orientation, race, \nmarital status, family or economic circumstances, education, origin or social condition, \ngenetic heritage, reduced capacity for work, disability, chronic illness, nationality, \nethnicity or race, territory of origin, language, religion, political or ideological \nconvictions and union membership. \n29. In accordance with D.L. nº 29/2001, of 3 of February, candidates with disabilities are \npreferred in case of equal classification, which prevails over any other legal \npreferences. The candidates must provide a declaration of honor with the respective \ndegree of incapacity, type of disability, and the communication/expression media to \nbe used in the selection process, under the legislation mentioned above. \n "
    },
    "https://www2.novasbe.unl.pt/Portals/0/Files/Openings/Research/CALL%20FOR%20DOCTORATE%20HIRING%20AAC%20julho%2020190819.pdf?ver=2019-07-19-101910-927": {
      "title": "2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee",
      "description": "Notice 11700/2019 \n \n \n \nNotice of an international public call for Doctorate hiring under the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, \n29th August \n \n1. Call identification \nThis call , for the recruitment of a Doctor ate to perform research activities on the \nscientific field of Economics, in an employment contract for an indefinite period under \nthe Portuguese Labour Code is raised, under the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, 29  August, \nfor the project “Land Use Changes at The Urban -Rural Interface: A Portuguese Case \nStudy” with the reference Projeto de IC&DT – AAC n.º 02/SAICT/2017. \n \n2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee \nof Faculdade de Economia/ Nova School of Business and Economics. \n \n3. Non admission for the reason of lack of absolute merit \nCandidates that do not obtain at least 50 points in a scale between 0 and 100 measuring \nthe seriation criteria will not be selected for lack of absolute merit. \n \n4. Applicable Law \nDecree-Law no. 57/206, 29 Aug ust, which approves the hiring regime of Doctorate s, \naiming to stimulate the scientific and technological job market in all knowledge fields \n(RJEC) \nLaw no. 57/2017, 29 August, that rules the first change of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016. \nLabor Code, approved by Law no. 7/2009, 12 February, in its current version. \n \n5. Under the article 16th of the Decree -Law no. 57/2016, the authorization of the \nGovernment members responsible for the Finance and Public Administration areas is \nnot needed, namely that defined in the no. 3 of the article 7th of the LTFP, the previous \npositive opinion of the Government members responsible for the Finance and Public \nAdministration areas, as written in the no. 5 of the article 30th of the LTFP and the \nprocedure for the recruitment of public workers on a requalification status, referred to \nat the article no. 265 of the LTFP. \n \n6. As stated in the article 13 th of the RJEC, the Call Jury has the following member \ncomposition: \n \n• Professor Maria Antonieta Cunha e Sá \n• Professor Sofia F. Franco \n• Professor Renato Rosa \n• Carina Silva, PhD \n \n \n7. The workplace is the facilities of the Faculdade de Economia/ School of Business and \nEconomics, without prejudice to any travelling justified by the job. \n \n8. The monthly salary is as defined in the no.1 of the article 15 th of the Law 57/2017, 19 \nJuly, corresponding to the le vel 33 of the “Tabela Remuneratória Única”, approved by \nthe ordinance no. 1553 -C/2008, 31 December: €2.128,34 (two thousand one hundred \nand twenty eight euros and thirty four cents). \n \n9. Will be admitted to this call any Portuguese, foreign or stateless candidate with a \nDoctoral degree in Economics or similar and a n adequate scientific and professional \ncurriculum. If the Doctoral degree was obtained in a non-Portuguese University it must \nobey to the stated in the Decree -Law no. 341/20107, 12 October, and any needed \nformalities must be completed until the end of the call. \n \n10. There are special requisites to admission to this call those defined in the previous \nnumber. \n \n11.  Under the terms of the ar ticle 5 th of the RJEC, the selection is done through the \nassessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates. \n \n12. The assessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates is done \nconsidering the relevance, quality and actuality of: \na) The scientific production of the last five years considered most relevant by the \ncandidate; \nb) The applied scientific activities, or practice based, developed on the last five years e \nconsidered by the candidate as the most impactful; \nc) The competencies of using different software below mentioned \nd) The activities of extension and of knowledge dissemination developed in the last \nfive years, namely on the context of culture and scientific practice promotion \nconsidered most relevant by the candidate; \n \n13. The five years period stated in the previous number may be extended by the Jury at a \ncandidate’s request if it is based on a scientific activity interruption due to socially \nprotected reasons, namely parental leave, serious or prolonged illness  and other \nsituations legally protected  \n \n14. The assessment criteria are: \n \na) On the scientific performance parameter, the publication in the Macroeconomics  \nfield with a strong computational and quantitative component in top peer-reviewed \nInternational journals . Preference will be given to candidates with experience in \nmore than one of these fields. \nb) On the applied research parameter, the participation in research projects in the \nEnvironmental and Natural Resources Economy field with a space dimension \ncomponent (knowledge of spatial econometrics technics). \nc) On the computational parameter, advanced knowledge of programing language s \nsuch as Stata, R, Python, as well as ArcGIS, QGIS, or other \nd) On the activities of work on projects, the assessment will be done through an \ninterview with the jury , mainly the fluency in English (writing and conversation), \ncommunication and interpersonal relationship competences, as well as team work \nand project management experience. \n  \n \n15. The final classification system of the candidates is done in a 0 to 100 scale, according to \nthe following evaluation table: \n \nCriterion Criterion \nweighting Criterion Scoring \nScientific production in the \nEnvironmental and Natural \nResources Economics field  \n10% \n• 10 or more publications in scientific \njournals classified on the ABS, ISI or \nSCOPUS lists - 100 \n• 5 or more publications in scientific \njournals classified on the ABS, ISI or \nSCOPUS lists - 90 \n• Less than 5 publications in scientific peer \nreviewed journals not classified on the \nABS, ISI or SCOPUS lists - 40 \n• Publications in scientific journals not \nclassified on the ABS, ISI or SCOPUS lists – \n10 \n• Non demonstrated ability to publish in \npeer reviewed journals – 0 \nApplied Research – \nparticipation in research \nprojects in the \nEnvironmental and Natural \nResources Economics field \n15% \n• Participation in applied research projects \nin the Environmental and Natural \nResources Economics field, with spatial \neconometrics techniques knowledge – \n100 \n• Participation in applied research projects \nin the Environmental and Natural \nResources Economics field - 80 \n• No participation in applied research \nprojects in the Environmental and Natural \nResources Economics field - 0 \nSoftware using experience I 15% \n• Knowledge of at least 2 of the following \ncomputing languages: Stata, R, Python – \n100 \n• Knowledge of only one of the following \ncomputing languages: Stata, R, Python – \n70 \n• Knowledge of Stata (only) – 40 \n• Absence of knowledge of the computing \nlanguages: Stata, R, Python - 0 \nSoftware using experience I 10% \n• Experience using software like ArcGIS, \nQGIS, among other – 100 \n• Absence of experience using software like \nArcGIS, QGIS, among other - 0 \nAttitude and work project \ncompetencies 50% \n• Demonstration of the sensibility needed \nfor a good project execution, as well as \nknowledge of the project field, assessed \nin an interview with the jury. A scale from \n0 (inadequate attitude and \ncompetencies) to 100 (excellent attitude \nand competencies) will be used. \n \n16. The admitted candidate will perform at least the following activities: \na) Analysis and use of longitudinal data bases of microeconomic data  \nb) Development and implementation of spatial econometric and causal inference \ntechniques using appropriate software as Stata and/or R \nc) Microeconomic data maping using geographical information systems (e.g. ArcGIS, \nQGIS or similar) \nd) Participation and promotion of activities within the project scope with other \ncolleagues and research groups. \ne) Participation in activities related to the project aims, namely those related to the \ncollecting and synthesis of bibliographic data and dissemination activities such as \nscientific papers preparation, presentations in conferences, seminars, workshops, \netc., as well as the organization of such events within the scope of the project. \n \n17. The jury deliberates through nominal voting justified according to the selection criteria \nadopted and publicized. Abstention is not allowed. \n \n18. The minutes of the jury meetings must contain a brief description of the issues \ndiscussed, as well as each member’s votes with justification, and candidates are entitled \nto read it if required. \n \n19. After the application of the selection criteria, the jury must elaborate the ranked list of \ncandidates with the respective classification. \n \n20. The final deliberation of the jury must be homologated by the Head of the Institution \nwho also decides on the hiring. \n \n21. Applications: \n21.1. Applications are formalized through an application form available to download \nat the Nova School of Business and Economics webpage  - \nhttps://www2.novasbe.unl.pt/en/about-us/join-our-school , addressed to the \nSchool’s Dean, containing the identification of the present Call, complete candidate \nname, names of father and mother, number and date of the identification \ndocument, fiscal number, date and place of birth, marital status, occupation, \nresidency data and contact data, including e-mail address and phone number. \n21.2. The candidate should also attach documents that make proof of the conditions \nstated in articles 10 and 12, namely: \na) Copy of the certificate or Diploma \nb) PhD Thesis \nc) Detailed curriculum vitae, structured in accordance with items from article 14 \nd) Other relevant documents  \n \n22. The candidates should present their application forms as well as the other documents \nrequested preferably in digital versions, PDF, to the e -mail address: \nresearchposition@novasbe.pt, personally at the Faculty Affairs Department of the Nova \nSchool of Business and Economics (“Serviço de Apoio ao Docente”), Rua da Holanda, nº \n1, 2775 -405 Carcavelos , during working hours or by post to the same address. The \napplications sent by post must be registered with rece ption proving, until the last day \nof the call opening, which is 6 working days after the publishing of the Call at the Diário \nda República, that is, until 26 July 2019. \n \n23. Candidates that do not dully formalize their applications or that do not make proof of \nthe Call requisites will be excluded. The jury is allowed to require of any candidate any \ndocument that makes proof of any declaration on the application. \n \n24. False declarations should be punished according to the law. \n \n25. The list of the accepted and excluded ca ndidates as well as the list with the final \nclassification must be posted in the School’s facilities, at Rua da Holanda, nº 1, 2775-405 \nCarcavelos, at the Universidade Nova de Lisboa and the School’s webpages, and the \ncandidates must be notified through e-mail with Delivery Report request. \n \n26. Previous audience and deadline for final decision: As stated in the article no. 121 of the \nAdministrative Proceedings Code (“Código do Procedimento Administrativo”), after \nbeing notified the candidates have 10 working da ys to reply. The final decision of the \njury must be taken during the 10 days after the deadline for applications. \n \n27. The current call is exclusively dedicated to fill the job position above mentioned and can \nbe terminated until the homologation of the candidates final ranked list. It will expire at \nthe moment that the job position is filled with the selected candidate. \n \n28. Nondiscrimination and equal access policy: Universidade N ova de Lisboa actively \npromotes a nondiscrimination and equal access policy, under which, no candidate shall \nbe prejudiced either favorable or unfavorable, deprived of any right or exempt from any \nduty, for reasons of, namely, descent, age, gender, sexual orientation, race, marital \nstatus, family or economic circumstances, education, origin or social condition, genetic \nheritage, reduced capacity for work, disability, chronic illness, nationality, ethnicity or \nrace, territory of origin, language, religion, political or ideological convictions and union \nmembership. \n29. In accordance with D.L. nº 29/2001, of 3 of February, candidates with disabilities are \npreferred in case of equal classification, which prevails over any other legal preferences. \nThe candidates must provide a declaration of honor with the respective degree of \nincapacity, type of disability, and the communication/expression media to be used in \nthe selection process, under the legislation mentioned above. \n \n \n "
