    "https://www.novasbe.unl.pt/Portals/0/Files/Openings/Research/CALL%20FOR%20DOCTORATE%20HIRING%208747_2020.pdf?_gl=1*1dkl70r*_up*MQ..*_ga*MTQ3NjQyMTUwOC4xNzg4Mjg5Nzc1*_ga_NRJH2682FN*czE3ODgyODk3NzMkbzEkZzAkdDE3ODgyODk3NzMkajYwJGwwJGg3NTg5MTkxNDk.": {
      "title": "2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee",
      "description": "Notice 8747/2020 \n \n \nNotice of an international public call for Doctorate hiring under the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, \n29th August \n \n1. Call identification \nThis call, for the recruitment of a Doctorate to perform research activities on the \nscientific field of Economics, Development Economics, in an employment contract for \nan indefinite period under the Portuguese Labour Code is raised, under the Decree-\nLaw no. 57/2016, 29 August, under the multiannual I&D 2020-2023 Funding, with \nreference UIDB/00124/2020. \n \n2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee \nof Faculdade de Economia/ Nova School of Business and Economics. \n \n3. Non admission for the reason of lack of absolute merit \nCandidates that do not obtain at least 50 points in a scale between 0 and 100 \nmeasuring the seriation criteria will not be selected for lack of absolute merit. \n \n4. Applicable Law \nDecree-Law no. 57/206, 29 August, which approves the hiring regime of Doctorates, \naiming to stimulate the scientific and technological job market in all knowledge fields \n(RJEC) \nLaw no. 57/2017, 29 August, that rules the first change of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016. \nLabor Code, approved by Law no. 7/2009, 12 February, in its current version. \n \n5. Under the article 16th of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, the authorization of the \nGovernment members responsible for the Finance and Public Administration areas is \nnot needed, namely that defined in the no. 3 of the article 7th of the LTFP, the \nprevious positive opinion of the Government members responsible for the Finance and \nPublic Administration areas, as written in the no. 5 of the article 30th of the LTFP and \nthe procedure for the recruitment of public workers on a requalification status, \nreferred to at the article no. 265 of the LTFP. \n \n6. As stated in the article 13th of the RJEC, the Call Jury has the following member \ncomposition: \n \n• Professor Miguel Luís Sousa de Almeida Ferreira, President of the juri \n• Professor Pedro Luís de Oliveira Martins Pita Barros \n• Professor Pedro Miguel da Cruz Correia Gardete \n \n7. The workplace is the facilities of the Faculdade de Economia/ School of Business and \nEconomics, without prejudice to any travelling justified by the job. \n \n8. The monthly salary is as defined in the no.1 of the article 15th of the Law 57/2017, 19 \nJuly, corresponding to the level 33 of the “Tabela Remuneratória Única”, approved by \nthe ordinance no. 1553-C/2008, 31 December: €2.128,34 (two thousand one hundred \nand twenty eight euros and thirty four cents). \n \n9. Will be admitted to this call any Portuguese, foreign or stateless candidate with a \nDoctoral degree in Economics and an adequate scientific and professional curriculum. \nIf the Doctoral degree was obtained in a non-Portuguese University it must obey to the \nstated in the Decree-Law no. 341/20107, 12 October, and any needed formalities must \nbe completed until the end of the call. \n \n10. There are special requisites to admission to this call those defined in the previous \nnumber. \n \n11.  Under the terms of the article 5th of the RJEC, the selection is done through the \nassessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates. \n \n12. The assessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates is done \nconsidering the relevance, quality and actuality of: \na) The scientific production of the last five years considered most relevant by the \ncandidate; \nb) The applied scientific activities, or practice based, developed on the last five years \ne considered by the candidate as the most impactful; \nc) The activities of extension and of knowledge dissemination developed in the last \nfive years, namely on the context of culture and scientific practice promotion \nconsidered most relevant by the candidate; \n \n13. The five years period stated in the previous number may be extended by the Jury at a \ncandidate’s request if it is based on a scientific activity interruption due to socially \nprotected reasons, namely parental leave, serious or prolonged illness and other \nsituations legally protected  \n \n14. The assessment criteria are: \n \na) On the Scientific Performance parameter, the scientific production over the last \nfive years considered most relevant by the candidate  \nb) On the applied research parameter, the participation in research over the last five \nyears considered most relevant by the candidate  \nc) On the activities of extension and of knowledge dissemination parameter, the \nparticipation in activities namely in the context of promoting culture and scientific \npractices, over the last 5 years, considered most relevant by the candidate. \n \n15. The final classification system of the candidates is done in a 0 to 100 scale, according \nto the following evaluation table:  \n  \nCriterion  Criterion \nweighting  \n Criterion Scoring  \nPublication on the field of \nEconomics.  60%  \n•  \n•  \n•  \nDemonstrated ability to publish in \njournals classified on ABS list as level 4 or \nabove – 100  \nDemonstrated ability to publish in \njournals classified on ABS list as level 3 – \n90  \nDemonstrated ability to publish in \njournals classified on ABS list as level 2 - \n40  \n  •  Demonstrated ability to publish in other \npeer reviewed journals– 10  \n  •  Non demonstrated ability to publish in \npeer reviewed journals  – 0  \nApplied Research – \nparticipation in research \nprojects in the field of \nEconomics   \n20%  \n•  \n•  \n•  \nParticipation in applied research projects \nof corporate finance – 100  \nParticipation in applied research projects \nin other fields of Finance – 50  \nNo participation in applied research \nprojects in any fields of Finance - 0  \nExtension and knowledge \ndissemination  20%  \n•  \n•  \n•  \nSupport in the decision making regarding \ncorporate finance at national and  \ninternational level – 100  \nSupport in the decision making regarding \ncorporate finance at international level–  \n50  \nSupport in the decision making regarding \ncorporate finance at national level – 40  \n  •  No support in the decision making \nregarding corporate finance at \ninternational or international level –0  \n \n16. The jury deliberates through nominal voting justified according to the selection criteria \nadopted and publicized. Abstention is not allowed. \n \n17. The minutes of the jury meetings must contain a brief description of the issues \ndiscussed, as well as each member’s votes with justification, and candidates are \nentitled to read it if required. \n \n18. After the application of the selection criteria, the jury must elaborate the ranked list of \ncandidates with the respective classification. \n \n19. The final deliberation of the jury must be homologated by the Head of the Institution \nwho also decides on the hiring. \n \n20. Applications: \n20.1. Applications are formalized through an application form available to download \nat the Nova School of Business and Economics webpage - \nhttp://www.novasbe.unl.pt/about-us/hr-management -, addressed to the \nSchool’s Dean, containing the identification of the present Call, complete \ncandidate name, number of the identification document, fiscal number, residency \ndata and contact data, including e-mail address and phone number. \n20.2. The candidate should also attach documents that make proof of the conditions \nstated in articles 10 and 11, namely: \na) Copy of the certificate or Diploma \nb) PhD Thesis \nc) Detailed curriculum vitae, structured in accordance with items from article 14 \nd) Other relevant documents  \n \n21. The candidates should present their application forms as well as the other documents \nrequested preferably in digital versions, PDF, to the e-mail address: \nresearchposition@novasbe.pt, personally at the Faculty Affairs Department of the \nNova School of Business and Economics (“Serviço de Apoio ao Docente”), Rua da \nHolanda, nº 1, 2775-405 Carcavelos, during working hours or by post to the same \naddress. The applications sent by post must be registered with reception proving, until \nthe last day of the call opening, which is 6 working days after the publishing of the Call \nat the Diário da República. \n \n22. Candidates that do not dully formalize their applications or that do not make proof of \nthe Call requisites will be excluded. The jury is allowed to require of any candidate any \ndocument that makes proof of any declaration on the application. \n \n23. False declarations should be punished according to the law. \n \n24. The list of the accepted and excluded candidates as well as the list with the final \nclassification must be posted in the School’s facilities, at Rua da Holanda, nº 1, 2775-\n405 Carcavelos, at the Universidade Nova de Lisboa and the School’s webpages, and \nthe candidates must be notified through e-mail with Delivery Report request. \n \n25. Previous audience and deadline for final decision: As stated in the article no. 121 of \nthe Administrative Proceedings Code (“Código do Procedimento Administrativo”), \nafter being notified the candidates have 10 working days to reply. The final decision of \nthe jury must be taken during the 10 days after the deadline for applications. \n \n26. The current call is exclusively dedicated to fill the job position above mentioned and \ncan be terminated until the homologation of the candidates final ranked list. It will \nexpire at the moment that the job position is filled with the selected candidate. \n \n27. Nondiscrimination and equal access policy: Universidade Nova de Lisboa actively \npromotes a nondiscrimination and equal access policy, under which, no candidate shall \nbe prejudiced either favorable or unfavorable, deprived of any right or exempt from \nany duty, for reasons of, namely, descent, age, gender, sexual orientation, race, \nmarital status, family or economic circumstances, education, origin or social condition, \ngenetic heritage, reduced capacity for work, disability, chronic illness, nationality, \nethnicity or race, territory of origin, language, religion, political or ideological \nconvictions and union membership. \n \n \n28. In accordance with D.L. nº 29/2001, of 3 of February, candidates with disabilities are \npreferred in case of equal classification, which prevails over any other legal preferences. \nThe candidates must provide a declaration of honor with the respective degree of \nincapacity, type of disability, and the communication/expression media to be used in \nthe selection process, under the legislation mentioned above. \n \nJune 1st, 2020 – The Dean, Prof. Doutor Daniel Abel Monteiro Palhares Traça. "
    },
    "https://www.novasbe.unl.pt/Portals/0/Files/Openings/Research/8_%20Aviso_125952020_ENG.pdf?_gl=1*1dkl70r*_up*MQ..*_ga*MTQ3NjQyMTUwOC4xNzg4Mjg5Nzc1*_ga_NRJH2682FN*czE3ODgyODk3NzMkbzEkZzAkdDE3ODgyODk3NzMkajYwJGwwJGg3NTg5MTkxNDk.": {
      "title": "2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee",
      "description": "Notice of an international public call for Doctorate hiring under the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, \n29th August \n \n1. Call identification \nThis call, for the recruitment of a Doctorate to perform research activities on the \nscientific field of Economics, Environmental Economics, in an employment contract for \nan indefinite period under the Portuguese Labour Code is raised, under the Decree-\nLaw no. 57/2016, 29 August, under the multiannual I&D 2020-2023 Funding, with \nreference UIDB/00124/2020. \n \n2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee \nof Faculdade de Economia/ Nova School of Business and Economics. \n \n3. Non admission for the reason of lack of absolute merit \nCandidates that do not obtain at least 50 points in a scale between 0 and 100 \nmeasuring the seriation criteria will not be selected for lack of absolute merit. \n \n4. Applicable Law \nDecree-Law no. 57/206, 29 August, which approves the hiring regime of Doctorates, \naiming to stimulate the scientific and technological job market in all knowledge fields \n(RJEC) \nLaw no. 57/2017, 29 August, that rules the first change of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016. \nLabor Code, approved by Law no. 7/2009, 12 February, in its current version. \n \n5. Under the article 16th of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, the authorization of the \nGovernment members responsible for the Finance and Public Administration areas is \nnot needed, namely that defined in the no. 3 of the article 7th of the LTFP, the \nprevious positive opinion of the Government members responsible for the Finance and \nPublic Administration areas, as written in the no. 5 of the article 30th of the LTFP and \nthe procedure for the recruitment of public workers on a requalification status, \nreferred to at the article no. 265 of the LTFP. \n \n6. As stated in the article 13th of the RJEC, the Call Jury has the following member \ncomposition: \n \n• Professor Miguel Luís Sousa de Almeida Ferreira, President of the juri; \n• Professor Pedro Luís de Oliveira Martins Pita Barros; \n• Professor Pedro Miguel da Cruz Correia Gardete. \n \n7. The workplace is the facilities of the Faculdade de Economia/ School of Business and \nEconomics, without prejudice to any travelling justified by the job. \n \n8. The monthly salary is as defined in the no.1 of the article 15th of the Law 57/2017, 19 \nJuly, corresponding to the level 33 of the “Tabela Remuneratória Única”, approved by \nthe ordinance no. 1553-C/2008, 31 December and on the level of Junior Researcher \n(PHD’s with little experience on the pos-doctoral research or without scientific \ncurriculum on the scientific field for which it is applying): €2.128,34 (two thousand one \nhundred and twenty eight euros and thirty four cents). \n \n9. Will be admitted to this call any Portuguese, foreign or stateless candidate with a \nDoctoral degree in Economics, or other interdisciplinary areas related with sustainable \ndevelopment politics with impact on the valuation of natural capital, and an adequate \nscientific and professional curriculum. If the Doctoral degree was obtained in a non-\nPortuguese University it must obey to the stated in the Decree-Law no. 341/20107, 12 \nOctober, and any needed formalities must be completed until the end of the call. \n \n10. There are special requisites to admission to this call those defined in the previous \nnumber. \n \n11.  Under the terms of the article 5th of the RJEC, the selection is done through the \nassessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates. \n \n12. The assessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates is done \nconsidering the relevance, quality and actuality of: \na) The scientific production of the last five years considered most relevant by the \ncandidate; \nb) The applied scientific activities, or practice based, developed on the last five years \ne considered by the candidate as the most impactful; \nc) The activities of extension and of knowledge dissemination developed in the last \nfive years, namely on the context of culture and scientific practice promotion \nconsidered most relevant by the candidate; \n \n13. The five years period stated in the previous number may be extended by the Jury at a \ncandidate’s request if it is based on a scientific activity interruption due to socially \nprotected reasons, namely parental leave, serious or prolonged illness and other \nsituations legally protected  \n \n14. The assessment criteria are: \n \na) On the Scientific Performance parameter, papers that reveal knowledge on the \narea of Economics, published on international top scientific journals with peer \nreview; \nb) On the applied research parameter, the participation in research projects of \nEconomics; \nc) On the activities of extension and of knowledge dissemination parameter, the \nparticipation in national and international activities namely in the context of \nEconomics. \n \n15. Under the 5th statement of the 5th article of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016 and the law \nno. 57/2017, the evaluation process may include an interview of the candidates or \nspecific candidates, duly selected by the jury. The final classification system of the \ncandidates is done in a 0 to 100 scale, according to the following evaluation table:  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n  \nCriterion  Criterion weighting   Criterion Scoring  \nScientific \nProduction that \nreveals \nknowledge on the \narea of \nEconomics \nand/or related \nwith the \nconservation of \nthe natural \ncapital  \nWithout interview: 60% \nWith interview: 50%  \n • Publish of 10 or more articles in scientific \njournals classified in the lists – ABS, ISI or \nSCOPUS - 100 \n• Publish of 5 or more articles in scientific \njournals classified in the lists – ABS, ISI or \nSCOPUS – 90 \n• Publish of less than 5 articles in scientific \njournals classified in the lists – ABS, ISI or \nSCOPUS – 70 \n• Publish on other scientific journals with \npeer review, non-classified on the lists - \nABS, ISI or SCOPUS – 50 \n• Inexistence of published papers in \nscientific journals with peer reviewed – 0  \n   \n   \nApplied Research \n– participation in \nresearch projects \nin the field of \nEnvironmental \nEconomics \nand/or related \nwith the \nconservation of \nthe natural \ncapital \n20%  \n • Participation in national and \ninternational applied research projects of \nEconomics – 100  \n• Participation in international applied \nresearch projects of Economics – 50 \n• Participation in national applied research \nprojects of Economics – 40  \n• No participation in applied research \nprojects in any fields of Economics - 0  \nExtension and \nknowledge \ndissemination  \n20% \n•  \n•  \n• \n \n  \nSupport in the decision making regarding \nEconomics at national and  \ninternational level – 100  \nSupport in the decision making regarding \nEconomics at international level–  \n50  \nSupport in the decision making regarding \nEconomics at national level – 40  \n• No support in the decision making \nregarding corporate finance at \ninternational or international level –0 \n \nInterview Without interview: 0% \nWith interview: 10% \n \n• Demonstration of the sensibility needed \nfor a good project execution, as well as \nknowledge of the project field, assessed \nin an interview with the jury. A scale \nfrom 0 (inadequate attitude and \ncompetencies) to 100 (excellent attitude \nand competencies) will be used.  \n \n \n16. The jury deliberates through nominal voting justified according to the selection criteria \nadopted and publicized. Abstention is not allowed. \n \n17. The minutes of the jury meetings must contain a brief description of the issues \ndiscussed, as well as each member’s votes with justification, and candidates are \nentitled to read it if required. \n \n18. After the application of the selection criteria, the jury must elaborate the ranked list of \ncandidates with the respective classification. \n \n19. The final deliberation of the jury must be homologated by the Head of the Institution \nwho also decides on the hiring. \n \n20. Applications: \n20.1. Applications are formalized through an application form available to download \nat the Nova School of Business and Economics webpage - \nhttps://www2.novasbe.unl.pt/en/about-us/join-our-school -, addressed to the \nSchool’s Dean, containing the identification of the present Call, complete \ncandidate name, number of the identification document, fiscal number, residency \ndata and contact data, including e-mail address and phone number. \n20.2. The candidate should also attach documents that make proof of the conditions \nstated in articles 10 and 11, namely: \na) Copy of the certificate or Diploma \nb) PhD Thesis \nc) Detailed curriculum vitae, structured in accordance with items from article 14 \nd) Other relevant documents  \n \n21. The candidates should present their application forms as well as the other documents \nrequested preferably in digital versions, PDF, to the e-mail address: \nresearchposition@novasbe.pt, personally at the Faculty Affairs Department of the \nNova School of Business and Economics (“Serviço de Apoio ao Docente”), Rua da \nHolanda, nº 1, 2775-405 Carcavelos, during working hours or by post to the same \naddress. The applications sent by post must be registered with reception proving, until \nthe last day of the call opening, which is 6 working days after the publishing of the Call \nat the Diário da República. \n \n22. Candidates that do not dully formalize their applications or that do not make proof of \nthe Call requisites will be excluded. The jury is allowed to require of any candidate any \ndocument that makes proof of any declaration on the application. \n \n23. False declarations should be punished according to the law. \n \n24. The list of the accepted and excluded candidates as well as the list with the final \nclassification must be posted in the School’s facilities, at Rua da Holanda, nº 1, 2775-\n405 Carcavelos, at the Universidade Nova de Lisboa and the School’s webpages, and \nthe candidates must be notified through e-mail with Delivery Report request. \n \n25. Previous audience and deadline for final decision: As stated in the article no. 121 of \nthe Administrative Proceedings Code (“Código do Procedimento Administrativo”), \nafter being notified the candidates have 10 working days to reply. The final decision of \nthe jury must be taken during the 10 days after the deadline for applications. \n \n26. The current call is exclusively dedicated to fill the job position above mentioned and \ncan be terminated until the homologation of the candidates final ranked list. It will \nexpire at the moment that the job position is filled with the selected candidate. \n \n27. Nondiscrimination and equal access policy: Universidade Nova de Lisboa actively \npromotes a nondiscrimination and equal access policy, under which, no candidate shall \nbe prejudiced either favorable or unfavorable, deprived of any right or exempt from \nany duty, for reasons of, namely, descent, age, gender, sexual orientation, race, \nmarital status, family or economic circumstances, education, origin or social condition, \ngenetic heritage, reduced capacity for work, disability, chronic illness, nationality, \nethnicity or race, territory of origin, language, religion, political or ideological \nconvictions and union membership. \n \n \n28. In accordance with D.L. nº 29/2001, of 3 of February, candidates with disabilities are \npreferred in case of equal classification, which prevails over any other legal preferences. \nThe candidates must provide a declaration of honor with the respective degree of \nincapacity, type of disability, and the communication/expression media to be used in \nthe selection process, under the legislation mentioned above. \n \n \n \nAugust 28th, 2020 – The Dean, Prof. Doutor Daniel Abel Monteiro Palhares Traça. "
    },
    "https://www.novasbe.unl.pt/Portals/0/Files/Openings/Research/2022/4_%20OpenCall%204137_2022_ENG.pdf?_gl=1*1dkl70r*_up*MQ..*_ga*MTQ3NjQyMTUwOC4xNzg4Mjg5Nzc1*_ga_NRJH2682FN*czE3ODgyODk3NzMkbzEkZzAkdDE3ODgyODk3NzMkajYwJGwwJGg3NTg5MTkxNDk.": {
      "title": "2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee",
      "description": "Notice 4137/2022 \nPublished on the 25th of February 2022 \n \n \nNotice of an international public call for Doctorate hiring under the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, \n29th August \n \n1. Call identification \nThis call, for the recruitment of one Doctorate to perform research activities on the \nscientific field of Economics with a strong quantitative component, in an employment \ncontract for an indefinite period under the Portuguese Labour Code is raised, under \nthe Decree-Law no. 57/2016, 29 August, for the project “Human capital spillovers” \nwith the reference EGE-ECO/29121/2017. \n \n2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee \nof Faculdade de Economia/ Nova School of Business and Economics. \n \n3. Non admission for the reason of lack of absolute merit \nCandidates that do not obtain at least 50 points in a scale between 0 and 100 \nmeasuring the seriation criteria will not be selected for lack of absolute merit. \n \n4. Applicable Law \nDecree-Law no. 57/206, 29 August, which approves the hiring regime of Doctorates, \naiming to stimulate the scientific and technological job market in all knowledge fields \n(RJEC) \nLaw no. 57/2017, 29 August, that rules the first change of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016. \nLabor Code, approved by Law no. 7/2009, 12 February, in its current version. \n \n5. Under the article 16th of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, the authorization of the \nGovernment members responsible for the Finance and Public Administration areas is \nnot needed, namely that defined in the no. 3 of the article 7th of the LTFP, the \nprevious positive opinion of the Government members responsible for the Finance and \nPublic Administration areas, as written in the no. 5 of the article 30th of the LTFP and \nthe procedure for the recruitment of public workers on a requalification status, \nreferred to at the article no. 265 of the LTFP. \n \n6. As stated in the article 13th of the RJEC, the Call Jury has the following member \ncomposition: \n \n• Professor Paulo M. M. Rodrigues, President of the Jury \n• Professor Pedro Portugal \n• Professor Paulo Guimarães  \n \n7. The workplace is the facilities of the Faculdade de Economia/ School of Business and \nEconomics, without prejudice to any travelling justified by the job. \n \n8. The monthly salary is as defined in the no.1 of the article 15th of the Law 57/2017, 19 \nJuly, corresponding to the level 33 of the “Tabela Remuneratória Única”, approved by \nthe ordinance no. 1553-C/2008, 31 December: €2.153.94 (two thousand one hundred \nand fifty three euros and ninety four cents). \n \n9. Will be admitted to this call any Portuguese, foreign or stateless candidate with a \nDoctoral degree in Economics or similar and a scientific and professional curriculum \nadequate to the job. If the Doctoral degree was obtained in a non-Portuguese \nUniversity it must obey to the stated in the Decree-Law no. 341/20107, 12 October, \nand any needed formalities must be completed until the end of the call. \n \n10. There are special requisites to admission to this call those defined in the previous \nnumber. \n \n11.  Under the terms of the article 5th of the RJEC, the selection is done through the \nassessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates. \n \n12. The assessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates is done \nconsidering the relevance, quality and actuality of: \na) The scientific production of the last five years considered most relevant by the \ncandidate; \nb) The applied scientific activities, or practice based, developed on the last five years \nand considered by the candidate as the most impactful; \nc) The activities of extension and of knowledge dissemination developed in the last \nfive years, namely on the context of culture and scientific practice promotion \nconsidered most relevant by the candidate; \n \n13. The five years period stated in the previous number may be extended by the Jury at a \ncandidate’s request if it is based on a scientific activity interruption due to socially \nprotected reasons, namely parental leave, serious or prolonged illness and other \nsituations legally protected  \n \n14. The assessment criteria are: \n \na) On the scientific performance parameter, the publication on the field of \nEconometrics or Statistics in top peer-reviewed International journals  \nb) On the applied research parameter, the participation in research projects in the field \nof Economics or Finance. \nc) On the computing parameter, advanced knowledge of programing languages \n(example: Python, Stata, R, MATLAB) \nd) On the activities of work on projects, the assessment will be done through an \ninterview with the jury \n. \n15. The final classification system of the candidates is done in a 0 to 100 scale, according \nto the following evaluation table: \n \nCriterion Criterion \nweighting Criterion Scoring \nScientific production in the \nfields of Econometrics, \nStatistics, Economics or \nFinance \n35% \n• Demonstrated ability to publish in \njournals classified on ABS list as level 4 or \nabove – 100 \n• Demonstrated ability to publish in \njournals classified on ABS list as level 3 – \n90 \n• Demonstrated ability to publish in \njournals classified on ABS list as level 2 -\n40 \n• Demonstrated ability to publish in other \npeer reviewed journals– 10 \n• Non demonstrated ability to publish in \npeer reviewed journals – 0 \nApplied Research – \nparticipation in research \nprojects in the fields of \nEconomics or Finance \n15% \n• Participation in applied research projects \nin the fields of Economics or Finance – \n100 \n• Participation in applied research projects \nin other fields – 50 \n• No participation in applied research \nprojects - 0 \nComputing 15% \n• Knowledge of all the following computing \nlanguages: Python, Stata, R, MATLAB – \n100 \n• Knowledge of some of the computing \nlanguages: Python, Stata, R, MATLAB – 50 \n• Absence of knowledge of any of the \ncomputing languages: Python, Stata, R, \nMATLAB. \nAttitude and work project \ncompetencies 35% \n• Demonstration of the sensibility needed \nfor a good project execution, as well as \nknowledge of the project field, assessed \nin an interview with the jury. A scale from \n0 (inadequate attitude and \ncompetencies) to 100 (excellent attitude \nand competencies) will be used. \n \n16. The admitted candidate will perform at least the following activities: \na) Microeconomics data analysis; \nb) Assistance on the development, analyses and test of econometrics tools; \nc) Participation in activities related to the project objectives, namely related to \nbibliography collection and synthesis and dissemination. \nd) Eventual participation in documents resulting from the project as co-author \n \n17. The jury deliberates through nominal voting justified according to the selection criteria \nadopted and publicized. Abstention is not allowed. \n \n18. The minutes of the jury meetings must contain a brief description of the issues \ndiscussed, as well as each member’s votes with justification, and candidates are \nentitled to read it if required. \n \n19. After the application of the selection criteria, the jury must elaborate the ranked list of \ncandidates with the respective classification. \n \n20. The final deliberation of the jury must be homologated by the Head of the Institution \nwho also decides on the hiring. \n \n21. Applications: \n21.1. Applications are formalized through an application form available to download \nat the Nova School of Business and Economics webpage - \nhttps://www2.novasbe.unl.pt/en/about-us/join-our-school -, addressed to the \nSchool’s Dean, containing the identification of the present Call, complete \ncandidate name, names of father and mother, number and date of the \nidentification document, fiscal number, date and place of birth, marital status, \noccupation, residency data and contact data, including e-mail address and phone \nnumber. \n21.2. The candidate should also attach documents that make proof of the conditions \nstated in articles 11 and 13, namely: \na) Copy of the certificate or Diploma \nb) PhD Thesis \nc) Detailed curriculum vitae, structured in accordance with items from article 14 \nd) Other relevant documents  \n \n22. The candidates should present their application forms as well as the other documents \nrequested preferably in digital versions, PDF, to the e-mail address: \nresearchposition@novasbe.pt, personally at the Faculty Affairs Department of the \nNova School of Business and Economics (“Serviço de Apoio ao Docente”), Rua da \nHolanda, nº 1, 2775-405 Carcavelos, during working hours or by post to the same \naddress. The applications sent by post must be registered with reception proving, until \nthe last day of the call opening, which is 20 working days after the publishing of the \nCall at the Diário da República. \n \n23. Candidates that do not dully formalize their applications or that do not make proof of \nthe Call requisites will be excluded. The jury can require of any candidate any \ndocument that makes proof of any declaration on the application. \n \n24. False declarations should be punished according to the law. \n \n25. The list of the accepted and excluded candidates as well as the list with the final \nclassification must be posted in the School’s facilities, at Rua da Holanda, nº 1, 2775-\n405 Carcavelos, at the Universidade Nova de Lisboa and the School’s webpages, and \nthe candidates must be notified through e-mail with Delivery Report request. \n \n26. Previous audience and deadline for final decision: As stated in the article no. 121 of \nthe Administrative Proceedings Code (“Código do Procedimento Administrativo”), \nafter being notified the candidates have 10 working days to reply. The final decision of \nthe jury must be taken during the 10 days after the deadline for applications. \n \n27. The current call is exclusively dedicated to fill the job position above mentioned and \ncan be terminated until the homologation of the candidates final ranked list. It will \nexpire at the moment that the job position is filled with the selected candidate. \n \n28. Nondiscrimination and equal access policy: Universidade Nova de Lisboa actively \npromotes a nondiscrimination and equal access policy, under which, no candidate shall \nbe prejudiced either favorable or unfavorable, deprived of any right or exempt from \nany duty, for reasons of, namely, descent, age, gender, sexual orientation, race, \nmarital status, family or economic circumstances, education, origin or social condition, \ngenetic heritage, reduced capacity for work, disability, chronic illness, nationality, \nethnicity or race, territory of origin, language, religion, political or ideological \nconvictions and union membership. \n29. In accordance with D.L. nº 29/2001, of 3 of February, candidates with disabilities are \npreferred in case of equal classification, which prevails over any other legal \npreferences. The candidates must provide a declaration of honor with the respective \ndegree of incapacity, type of disability, and the communication/expression media to \nbe used in the selection process, under the legislation mentioned above. \n "
    },
    "https://www.novasbe.unl.pt/Portals/0/Files/Openings/Research/2022/1_%20Edital_5048_ENG.pdf?_gl=1*1dkl70r*_up*MQ..*_ga*MTQ3NjQyMTUwOC4xNzg4Mjg5Nzc1*_ga_NRJH2682FN*czE3ODgyODk3NzMkbzEkZzAkdDE3ODgyODk3NzMkajYwJGwwJGg3NTg5MTkxNDk.": {
      "title": "2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee",
      "description": " \nNotice 5048/2022 \nPublished on March 10th \n \nNotice of an international public call for Doctorate hiring under the Decree-Law no. 57/2016, \n29th August \n \n1. Call identification \nThis call, for the recruitment of a Doctorate to perform research activities on the \nscientific field of Economics, in an employment contract for an indefinite period under \nthe Portuguese Labour Code is raised, under the Decree -Law no. 57/2016, 29 August, \nfor the project “Choosing a Business model in the social entrepreneurship context: \ntypology of current practices and the influence of the social entrepreneur’s background” \nwith the reference EGE-ECO/31213/2017. \n \n2. The decision to open this call was taken by the Faculty Council Coordinator Committee \nof Faculdade de Economia/ Nova School of Business and Economics. \n \n3. Non admission for the reason of lack of absolute merit \nCandidates that do not obtain at least 50 points in a scale between 0 and 100 measuring \nthe seriation criteria will not be selected for lack of absolute merit. \n \n4. Applicable Law \nDecree-Law no. 57/206, 29 August, which approves the hiring regime of Doctorates, \naiming to stimulate the scientific and technological job market in all knowledge fields \n(RJEC) \nLaw no. 57/2017, 29 August, that rules the first change of the Decree-Law no. 57/2016. \nLabor Code, approved by Law no. 7/2009, 12 February, in its current version. \n \n5. Under the article 16th of the Decree -Law no. 57/2016, the authorization of the \nGovernment members responsible for the Finance and Public Administration areas is \nnot needed, namely that defined in the no. 3 of the article 7th of the LTFP, the previous \npositive opinion of the Government members responsible for the Finance and Public \nAdministration areas, as written in the no. 5 of the article 30th of the LTFP and the \nprocedure for the recruitment of public workers on a requalification status, referred to \nat the article no. 265 of the LTFP. \n \n6. As stated in the article 13 th of the RJEC, the Call Jury has the following member \ncomposition: \n \n• Professor Susana Peralta, President of the Jury \n• Professor Pedro Pita Barros \n• Professor Ana Balcão Reis \n• Professor Cátia Batista \n \n7. The workplace is the facilities of the Faculdade  de Economia/ School of Business and \nEconomics, without prejudice to any travelling justified by the job. \n \n8. The monthly salary is as defined in the no.1 of the article 15 th of the Law 57/2017, 19 \nJuly, corresponding to the level 33 of the “Tabela Remunerató ria Única”, approved by \nthe ordinance no. 1553 -C/2008, 31 December: € 2.153,94 (two thousand one hundred \nand fifty three euros and ninety four cents). \n \n9. Will be admitted to this call any Portuguese, foreign or stateless candidate with a \nDoctoral degree in Ec onomics or similar and a scientific and professional curriculum \nadequate to the job. If the Doctoral degree was obtained in a non-Portuguese University \nit must obey to the stated in the Decree -Law no. 341/20107, 12 October, and any \nneeded formalities must be completed until the end of the call. \n \n10. There are special requisites to admission to this call those defined in the previous \nnumber. \n \n11.  Under the terms of the article 5 th of the RJEC, the selection is done through the \nassessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates. \n \n12. The assessment of the scientific and professional curriculum of the candidates is done \nconsidering the relevance, quality and actuality of: \na) The scientific production of the last five years considered most relevant by the \ncandidate; \nb) The applied scientific activities, or practice based, developed on the last five years \nand considered by the candidate as the most impactful; \nc) The activities of extension and of knowledge dissemination developed in the last \nfive years, namely on the context of culture and scientific practice promotion \nconsidered most relevant by the candidate; \n \n13. The five years period stated in the previous number may be extended by the Jury at a \ncandidate’s request if it is based on a scientific activity interruption due to socially \nprotected reasons, namely parental leave, serious or prolonged illness and other \nsituations legally protected  \n \n14. The assessment criteria are: \n \na) In the field of scientific production, the candidate must present evidence of knowledge \nof theoretical modelling, empirical analysis of causal inference and design of field \nexperiences, in the are a of political economy. It must also have scientific articles \nsubmitted or published in international peer -reviewed journals. The candidate's \ndoctoral thesis must deal with topics of empirical evaluation of public policies; \nb) In the field of applied research, the candidate should have experience in implementing \nexperiments, managing research teams and participating in research projects in the area \nof Political Economy; must demonstrate knowledge of the STATA econometric software; \nc) In terms of extension and dis semination of knowledge, the candidate must have \nparticipated in scientific conferences and summer schools, have experience of \ninteracting with research centers in the area of political economy and also experience \nof applied analysis of public policies. \n \n15. The final classification system of the candidates is done in a 0 to 100 scale, according to \nthe following evaluation table: \n \nCriterion Criterion \nweighting Criterion Scoring \nScientific production in the \narea of economic policies 45% \n• Thesis in the area of empirical \nevaluation of public policies – 100 \n• Publication or submission of articles \nor publication in scientific journals \nclassified in the ABS list with level 3/4 \n– 80 \n• Publication or submission of articles \nor publication in scientific journals \nclassified in the ABS list with level 2 – \n40 \n• Other publications in peer -reviewed \nscientific journals – 10 \n• No publication in peer -reviewed \nscientific journals – 0 \nApplied research in the area \nof economic policies 40% \n• Participation in research projects in \nthe area of political economy - 100 \n• Participation in applied research \nprojects in other areas of public sector \neconomics – 50 \n• Design and implementation of field \nexperiences, software knowledge \nnecessary for applied research \n(STATA) – 40 \n• No participation in applied research \nprojects in areas of public sector \neconomics – 0 \nExtension and dissemination \nof knowledge 15% \n• Interaction with international \nresearch teams in the area of applied \neconomics - 100 \n• Participation in scientific conferences \nand summer schools - 50 \n• No participation in scientific \nconferences - 0 \n \n16. The jury deliberates through nominal voting justified according to the selection criteria \nadopted and publicized. Abstention is not allowed. \n \n17. The minutes of the jury meetings must conta in a brief description of the issues \ndiscussed, as well as each member’s votes with justification, and candidates are entitled \nto read it if required. \n \n18. After the application of the selection criteria, the jury must elaborate the ranked list of \ncandidates with the respective classification. \n \n19. The final deliberation of the jury must be homologated by the Head of the Institution \nwho also decides on the hiring. \n \n20. Applications: \n20.1. Applications are formalized through an application form available to downlo ad \nat the Nova School of Business and Economics webpage - \nhttps://www2.novasbe.unl.pt/en/about-us/join-our-school -, addressed to the \nSchool’s Dean, containing the identification of the present Call, complete candidate \nname, names of father and mother, number and date of the identification \ndocument, fiscal number, date and place of birth, marital status, occupation, \nresidency data and contact data, including e-mail address and phone number. \n20.2. The candidate should also attach documents that make proof of the conditions \nstated in articles 11 and 13, namely: \na) Copy of the certificate or Diploma \nb) PhD Thesis \nc) Detailed curriculum vitae, structured in accordance with items from article 14 \nd) Other relevant documents  \n \n21. The candidates should present their application forms as well as the other documents \nrequested preferably in digital versions, PDF, to the e -mail address: \nresearchposition@novasbe.pt, perso nally at the Faculty Affairs Department of the \nNova School of Business and Economics (“Serviço de Apoio ao Docente”), Rua da \nHolanda, nº 1, 2775 -405 Carcavelos, during working hours or by post to the same \naddress. The applications sent by post must be registered with reception proving, until \nthe last day of the call opening, which is 6 working days after the publishing of the Call \nat the Diário da República. \n \n22. Candidates that do not duly formalize their applications or that do not make proof of \nthe Call requisites will be excluded. The jury can require of any candidate any document \nthat makes proof of any declaration on the application. \n \n23. False declarations should be punished according to the law. \n \n24. The list of the accepted and excluded candidates as well as th e list with the final \nclassification must be posted in the School’s facilities, at Rua da Holanda, nº 1, 2775-405 \nCarcavelos, at the Universidade Nova de Lisboa and the School’s webpages, and the \ncandidates must be notified through e-mail with Delivery Report request. \n \n25. Previous audience and deadline for final decision: As stated in the article no. 121 of the \nAdministrative Proceedings Code (“Código do Procedimento Administrativo”), after \nbeing notified the candidates have 6 working days to reply. The final decision of the jury \nmust be taken during the 10 days after the deadline for applications. \n \n26. The current call is exclusively dedicated to fill the job position above mentioned and can \nbe terminated until the homologation of the candidates final ranked list. It will expire at \nthe moment that the job position is filled with the selected candidate. \n \n27. Nondiscrimination and equal access policy: Universidade Nova de Lisboa actively \npromotes a nondiscrimination and equal access policy, under which, no candidate shall \nbe prejudiced either favorable or unfavorable, deprived of any right or exempt from any \nduty, for reasons of, namely, descent, age, gender, sexual orientation, race, marital \nstatus, family or economic circumstances, education, origin or social condition, genetic \nheritage, reduced capacity for work, disability, chronic illness, nationality, ethnicity or \nrace, territory of origin, language, religion, political or ideological convictions and union \nmembership. \n \n \nIn accordance with D.L. nº 29/2001, of 3 of February, candida tes with disabilities are preferred \nin case of equal classification, which prevails over any other legal preferences. The candidates \nmust provide a declaration of honor with the respective degree of incapacity, type of disability, \nand the communication/exp ression media to be used in the selection process, under the \nlegislation mentioned above. "
    },
    "https://www.novasbe.unl.pt/Portals/0/Files/Openings/Research/2022/1_%20Template_9172_ResearchAssistant_ENG.pdf?_gl=1*1dkl70r*_up*MQ..*_ga*MTQ3NjQyMTUwOC4xNzg4Mjg5Nzc1*_ga_NRJH2682FN*czE3ODgyODk3NzMkbzEkZzAkdDE3ODgyODk3NzMkajYwJGwwJGg3NTg5MTkxNDk.": {
      "title": "THE HIRING OF A RESEARCH ASSISTANT UNDER REGULATION 393/2018 OF JUNE 28",
      "description": "1 \n \n \nNOTICE OF THE OPENING OF THE INTERNATIONAL SELECTION COMPETITION PROCEDURE FOR \nTHE HIRING OF A RESEARCH ASSISTANT UNDER REGULATION 393/2018 OF JUNE 28 \n \n1. Call identification: \nThis call, for a position of research assistant to carry out scientific research activities, in \nthe scientific areas of Finance, in an employment contract for an indefinite period under \nthe Portuguese Labour Code is raised , under the Regulation on careers, the recruitment \nand empl oyment contracts of researchers under the employment contract regime of \nUniversidade Nova de Lisboa, Regulation 393/2018, of 28 June, for the Project \n“Financial Constraints, Public Policies and Firm Outcomes ” with reference  \nPTDC/EGE-OGE/4714/2021. \n2. The decision to open this call was taken at a meeting of the Coordinating Committee of \nthe Scientific Council of the Faculty of Economics – Nova School of Business and \nEconomics. \n3. No admission for lack of absolute merit \nCandidates who, on a rating scale between 0 and 100 of the respective ranking criteria, \ndo not obtain 50 will not be admitted to the competition due to lack of absolute merit. \n4. Applicable legislation \nThe hiring of the Research Assistant will be carried out through an uncertain resolution \nterm, to be concluded under the terms of the Labor Code, approved by Law no. 7/2009, \nof 12 February, in its current wording and by Regulation no. 393/2018 published in \nDiário da República no. 123, 2nd series of June 28, 2018. In accordance with article 12 \nof Regulation no. 393/2018, the call’s Jury has the following member composition: \n• Miguel Ferreira, as President \n• Francisco Queiró \n• Cátia Batista \n5. The workplace is located on the facilities of the Faculty of Economics/School of Business \nand Economics, without prejudice to travel inherent to the exercise of functions. \n6. The monthly remuneration to be attributed to the Research Assistant is that provided \nfor at the l evel 45A, 5th position of the table annexed to Regulation No. 393/2018, in  \nexclusivity in the amount of €2 779,27. \n2 \n \n7. National, foreign and stateless candidates who hold the degree of Master in Finance or \nrelated. If the master's degree has been awarded by a foreign higher education  \ninstitution, it must comply with the provisions of Decree-Law No. candidacy. \n8. The special requirements for admission to competition are those defined in the previous \npoint. \n9. The selection of the Research Assistant to be hired will be carried  out through the \nevaluation of their scientific and curricular path, in accordance with Article 37(1) of \nDecree-Law No. 124/99 of 20 April, which approves Scientific Research Career Statute \nand Regulation No. 393/2018 published in Diário da República No. 1 23, 2nd Series of \nJune 28, 2018, with the following selection criteria: \na) Master in Finance \nb) Experience in public policy evaluation \n \nThe jury may choose to include, as a second selection method, an Interview, which is \nexclusively intended to clarify aspects r elated to the candidates' experience, with a \nweight of 20%. All candidates, approved on absolute merit, are subject to the evaluation \nof the scientific and curricular path to be carried out according to the criteria and \nweightings defined in point “CV Evaluation”. However, they will only be admitted to \nthe Interview, if the jury decides to resort to it, and the 2 approved candidates and best \npositioned in the ranking resulting from the evaluation of the scientific and curricular \npath are ranked in it. \n \n10. The final classification system for candidates is expressed on a scale from 0 to 100, \naccording to the following evaluation table: \n \nCriterion Criterion weighting \nCV Evaluation 80% \nExperience in Public Policy Evaluation 20% \n \nHaving an interview, this will weight 20%, and the criterion “CV Evaluation”, 60%. \n \n11. The chosen person will perform, at least, the following tasks: \na) Collaboration in research about link between government-banks-firms \nb) Collaboration in research about effect of education on firm performance \n \n3 \n \n12. The jury decides through nominal voting based on the adopted and published selection \ncriteria, with no abstentions allowed. \n13. Minutes of the jury meetings are drawn up containing a summary of what took place \nthere, as well as the votes cast by e ach of the members and the respective reasons, \nbeing made available to candidates whenever requested. \n14. After completing the application of the selection criteria, the jury proceeds to draw up \nthe ordered list of candidates with their respective classification. \n15. The final decision of the jury is approved by the top manager of the institution, who is \nalso responsible for deciding on the hiring. \n16. Formalization of nominations: \n16.1. Applications are formalized upon request, available on the website of the \nFaculty of Economics/School of Business and Economics \n(https://www2.novasbe.unl.pt/en/about-us/join-our-school) addressed to the \nDirector, which includes the identification of this notice, full n ame, affiliation, \nidentity card number and date, Citizen's card, or civil identification number, tax \nidentification number, date and place of birth, marital status, occupation, \nresidence and contact address, including email address and telephone number. \n16.2. The application is accompanied by proof of the conditions set out in points 10 \nand 12 for admission to this competition, namely: \na) Copy of certificate or diploma; \nb) Detailed CV; \nc) Other relevant documents. \n17. Candidates submit their requirements and supporting docume nts, preferably in digital \nformat, in PDF format, to the email address faculty.recruitment@novasbe.pt , in person \nat the support service for teachers of the Faculty of Economics / School of Business and \nEconomics, Campus de Carcavelos, Rua da Holanda, nº1,  2775-405 Carcavelos, during \noffice hours, or by post to the same address. When sent by post, the mail must be \nregistered, with acknowledgment of receipt, sent by the last day of the deadline for \nopening the tender, which is set at 15 business days after the publication of this notice. \n18. Candidates who incorrectly formalize their application or who do not meet the \nrequirements required in this competition are excluded from admission to the \ncompetition. The jury has the right to require any candidate, in case of doubt, to present \ndocuments proving their statements. \n19. False statements made by candidates will be punished in accordance with the law. \n4 \n \n20. The list of admitted and excluded candidates as well as the final classification list are \nposted on the premises located at the Campus de Carcavelos, Rua da Holanda, nº 1, \n2775-405 Carcavelos, published on the websites of Universidade Nova de Lisboa and the \nFaculty of Economics. / School of Business and Economics, candidates being notified by \nemail with receipt of delivery of the notification. \n21. Prior hearing and deadline for Final Decision: Under the terms of article 121 of the \nAdministrative Procedure Code, after being notified, candidates have 10 working days \nto comment. Within a maximum period of 10 days from the deadline for the submission \nof indictments, the final decisions of the jury are made. \n22. This competition is exclusively intended to fill the vacancy indicated and  may be \nterminated until the approval of the final ranking list of candidates and expiring with the \nrespective occupation of the job on offer. \n23. Policy of non -discrimination and equal access: Universidade Nova de Lisboa actively \npromotes a policy of non-discrimination and equal access, so that no candidate can be \nprivileged, disadvantaged or deprived of any right or exempt from any duty on grounds, \nin particular, of ancestry, age, sex, sexual orientation, marital status, family situation, \neconomic situation, education, origin or social condition, genetic heritage, ability work, \ndisability, chronic illness, nationality, ethnic or racial origin, territory of origin, language, \nreligion, political or ideological beliefs and trade union membership. \n24. Pursuant to Decree -Law nº 29/2001, of February 3, candidates with disabilities have \npreference in equality of classification, which prevails over any other legal preference. \nCandidates must declare on the application form, under oath, the respective degree of \ndisability, the type of disability and the means of communication/expression to be used \nin the selection process, in accordance with the aforementioned diploma. "
    }
  },
